4.5,"[size=3][font=Garamond]Cool. Had Christmas break the past 2 weeks and managed to watch a couple of movies. 
 
 Life Aquatic With Steve Zissou (Wes Anderson)
 Million Dollar Baby (Clint Eastwood)
 Meet the Fockers (Jay Roach)
 In Good Company (Paul Weitz)
 
 The Life Aquatic. Very good comedy. Character development was pretty good, but I would have to say the ending was pretty anti-climactic. I read the plot summary on the Arclight site and it said something like ""Man loses partner to shark and seeks revenge"". Yeah that's how it started but the movie just evolved into something different. Watched @  Pacific Theaters at the Grove
 [/font][/size]
 [size=3][font=Garamond]Million Dollar Baby. Definitely excellent. It seemed sorta slow down towards the end but its natural. Very saddening, but did the writer really know the rules in boxing? I guess this is a bit of spoiler alert but I dont think I'm giving too much away....How in the hell did that chick get all those cheap shots in? I remember Roy Jones Jr getting his first loss, a DQ, because he knocked that dude Montell Griffin out when he already had kneeing down. I remember at least like 3 cheap shots/illegal hits. I'd go along with the ""suspension of disbelief"" but that's pretty unacceptable. I know they were trying to make it fit the story/ending but they could've worked around it you know? oh well. [/font][/size][size=3][font=Garamond]Watched @  Pacific Theaters at the Grove[/font][/size]
 [size=3][font=Garamond]
 Meet the Fockers. Yeah it was funny. No story at all, not even worth paying attention to. The humor is very sexually crude, sometimes childish, but funny at that. I guess it's recommendable. [/font][/size][size=3][font=Garamond]Watched @  Pacific Theaters at the Grove[/font][/size]
 [size=3][font=Garamond] 
 In Good Company. I just loved it. I know it may not seem that great to many others and that a lot of people think it's just an average-below par comedy, but I thought it was awesome. The characters were just so human...but we don't really see anyone that matters who throws a fit or gets pissed a ton. I can't really explain why I like it. I would say that there is no real conflict here...but that's fine. Ending was blah....but that's fine as well. I just couldn't get it out of my mind so I had to watch it again. The fact that it was funny (to me) made it easier to watch again. I probably plan on watching it again in wide release. [/font][/size][size=3][font=Garamond]Watched @  AMC Century 14.[/font][/size]
