5.0,"[center][img]http://imagecache2.allposters.com/images/153/1033881.jpg[/img][/center]
 

[left]Clint Eastwood's followup to Mystic River does not disappoint. The story is very moving with very good character development. Eastwood, Swank, and Freeman all give Oscar worthy performances and give the audience characters with heart and feeling that make them easy to cheer for and relate to.... The movie may be about boxing, but it is really about people, their dreams, and how friends help us achieve them. Million Dollar Baby also deals with guilt and accountability with our closest family/friends. When we become so involved in their lives where we are encouraging and pushing them, if they fail or fall short....then we fail too in our own eyes. Some of us feel responsible because we were the ones doing the pushing, but is it really our fault? I guess it all depends on how you look at it.[/left]

[left]This movie was very well produced and extremely well acted. It should get many awards/nominations in the upcoming months and they would be deserved.[/left]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-01-07","","RT","900673739"
4.0,"[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/million_dollar_baby/_group_photos/clint_eastwood8.jpg[/img]
 
I'll be damned if Million Dollar Baby didn't jump from one cliche to the other yet for for some reason it works. Eastwood's film is as stubborn as the character he plays. It does what you expect it to, does it well, and leaves you not caring that you weren't suprised. Its a well structured drama in the classical sense and doesn't take any lunges it shouldn't have. Its like I need someone to slap some sense into me and tell me what is wrong with this film. I can see all its errors but they didn't stop me from completely enjoying the story and the characters. The humor is obvious and nothing special, neither is the story, and really neither are the characters. But it works. I know I sound silly but whatever. Thats all I have to say about Million Dollar Baby.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2005-01-08","","RT","900621574"
