3.5,"[b]Million Dollar Baby:[/b]  Very well-acted, Morgan Freeman and Hillary Swank especially.  Simplistic in many ways - the plot is (mostly) conventional, the filming nothing fancy.  But it doesn't need embellishment, the performances are enough.  It isn't as moving as [b]Mystic River[/b], simply for the sake of comparison to another Eastwood film, but it still packs a bit of a punch.
 
[b]House of Flying Daggers:[/b]  The more of this movie I watched, the less I liked it.  My suggestion is to leave after 90 minutes and miss the ludicrous ending, which goes on forever and accomplishes nothing emotionally.  As he did with [b]Hero[/b], Zhang Yimou puts in some incredible visuals, great use of color, and kickass action.  And also like Hero, the story falls apart at the end.  This time, however, the style can't overcome the substance (even though Zhang Ziyi turns in a pretty good performance).  Here's my advice for your next movie, Yimou:
[spoiler] How about not having everybody die at the end for a change?  Seriously, whatever hard-on you have for Greecian/Shakesperian tragedy, lose it.  You can't pull it off.[/spoiler]","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2005-01-10","","RT","900601405"
