 Hilary Swank puts on the most complete performance of her acting career. It is no wonder why the Hollywood Foreign Press awarded her the Best Actress Golden Globe last night. While watching the film, you feel the emotion her character Maggie is going through. Now I can't forget about the superb Morgan Freeman. Like always, he puts on a great performance & better yet, he narrates throughout the film. So if you are looking for a great film, then look no further and experience the masterpiece that is [i]Million Dollar Baby.[/i]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-01-17","","RT","900676609"
4.5,"At first I was kind of down on the film just because it was so depressing - I was numb when I came out of the theater; I wanted to come home and just get drunk, and I don't even drink - that's how depressed I was.  I had no idea what to even say about the film.  Good thing I waited until today to write the review, because thinking about it a little more gave me a lot more respect for what Eastwood did - it's a film that's downbeat without ever feeling like it's cheaply going for sentiment.  The emotions are raw and earnest, never maudlin.  I still deduct a few points because it goes on a bit long and one of the subplots is out of place in its comic relief nature, but it's an excellent film that is a lock for my eventual top ten.
 
