2.5,"the aviator: the first movie i saw this year and a good one at that. i was a bit reluctant to see it since the cgs in the preview looked a bit hokey and gangs of ny ruined itself, but i actually found myself enjoying it more than most of the movies i saw in december. better pacing than gangs, and visually impressive (those party scenes were nice! and rufus wainright is awesome!). acting was pretty good but i felt that leo and cate were never able to fully absorb into their characters... and i laughed when i found out alec baldwin was playing a ""juan"" haha. not that alec's acting was bad... just that alec? as juan? haha ok maybe i'm the only person who finds that funny. oh and the ending felt a little off but it was appropriate i guess..
 
bad education: yay! gael garcia bernal is such a great actor! you may have assumed it before, but this movie definitely confirms how much gael truly loves acting. as for the movie in general, i'm not sure how strong this movie would have been if he hadn't been in it.. many would feel that the story telling was a bit messy and at times superfluous. i guess everything becomes purposeful by the end, but the unfolding of events is slightly sloppy in execution? i'm not too sure how to explain.. i was never very articulate! bah! but i guess what i'm trying to say is that despite the vibrant scenes and almodovar's knack for focusing on details that we ourselves would have noticed if we lived inside the movie, bad education never makes that much of an emotional impact. there's a distance to it; and while this may have been intentional, i think it diminishes the movie's overall effect
 
house of flying daggers: such a pretty movie! and the scenes between zhang ziyi and takeshi kaneshiro are so genuinely sweet that they turn me to mush. unfortunately, the ending is so unintentionally funny HAHA. and geezus! what ever happened to the original story? it's like zhang yimou turned all shakespeare on us! and not in a good way! i'm tempted to give the movie a 10 anyways cuz it was so beautiful and entertaining, but that cheese at the end is preventing me from doing so. booooo ><! and i think i was a bit too snobby when i first started this journal. if this movie gets a 9, then hero should definitely get higher than an 8. but i'm too lazy to go back and adjust all my ratings.. it's not like i get paid for this anyway haha
 
