5.0,"[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/million_dollar_baby/_group_photos/clint_eastwood6.jpg[/img]
  
 This film is great on all levels. I remember the first time I saw a trailer for this movie. I thought it looked really cheesy and wouldn't be that good. I couldn't have been more wrong it was great on all levels. I think the story is quite obvious but I will say a little bit about it. Clint Eastwood owns a gym and trains boxers. Hilary Swank comes to his gym and wants Clint to train her. 
 The performances by everyone involved are great. Even people that have like fifteen minutes of screen time are perfectly cast. I thought the best performance in the film was Morgan Freeman he has a supporting role but is excellent in that role. It's probably his second best performance behind Driving Miss Daisy. Not to take anything away from Hilary Swank or Clint Eastwood. They both deserve the praise they are getting as well. The screenplay was also very good. The movie will make you laugh and cry at the sametime. Not to mention the fact that there isn't a bad moment in the entire film. I also loved Clint's use of lighting in this film as the director. It kind of reminded me of the way they used lighting in old film noir. Not to say that this is anything like film noir. Actually the cinematography in this film is excellent overall, but I just wanted to point out the lighting as the strongpoint. Overall I think this should and will win best picture. This is a film not to be missed by anyone. Boxing fan or not this movie is much deeper than you can imagine. So run out and see it immediately!","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-02-14","","RT","900625067"
