[b][font=Times New Roman][size=3][i]Hotel Rwanda[/i] (Terry George, 2004)
Entertainment Value: 5/10 :rotten: 
Film Quality: 8/10 :fresh: [/size][/font][/b]
 
[b][font=Times New Roman][size=3]Not up to par with the best films of its type, but I guess it's unfair of me to compare George's effort with a masterpiece like [i]Schindler's List[/i]. Although the movie is just trying to be true to its source, I easily become bored with a film that is this static with its tone. The constant sadness and depressing mood is only broken for short times with a bit of suspense (and sometimes shock). It's a good adaptation of a story that needed to be told but it doesn't capture the horror of the tragedy well enough to bring attention to it.[/size][/font][/b]
 
[b][font=Times New Roman][size=3][i]Million Dollar Baby[/i] (Clint Eastwood, 2004)
Entertainment Value: 7/10 :fresh: 
Film Quality: 9/10 :fresh: [/size][/font][/b]
 
[b][font=Times New Roman][size=3]I'm not a fan of Clint Eastwood. I generally dislike his style (or lack of) in filmmaking. Surprisingly, though, this film works with most of his mundane directing. It's interesting to think about it now in hindsight and realize that the film didn't offer anything that new or original and in fact played off of some of the most overused ideas in Hollywood. Things like Maggie's attitude, her past, her relationship with her family, Frank and Maggie's relationship, Danger's character, and pretty much everything else is very ""by the books"". But some good acting and a film that never looses its serious tone no matter what stereotypes or clichés it uses ends up rising above all the melodrama associated with these things and creates something very real that you move (emotionally) with throughout the film.[/size][/font][/b]","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2005-02-16","","RT","900637649"
4.0,"fuck im [u]paranoid[/u]. seriously...i want it to go away. lately....ive been hanging out with Alana frequently. She likes me but she just broke up with her boyfriend Derek, and she [b]doesnt know what she wants[/b]. When we went out we didnt last very long but i dont know. Sometimes i doubt i like her...sometimes i think its [i]lust[/i] or something. We talk in phone usually twice a day after school....I think of her frequently, we hang out in school... before, nutrition break and lunch. Sometimes she doesnt spend the whole break with me but i guess i understand. She leaves her friends to hang out with me. If i put myself on her spot i guess I'd want to go back with my friends sometimes. Derek is [color=black]out[/color] of the picture but, I've been hearing about her first boyfriend[i] German[/i], who supposedly was really special. Well all ive heard is that they still talk and i read a note on her notebook that was to one of Alana's friends. It said that her and Derek didnt look too good, and that she still talked to German and that she was gonna look for him in the park. However, it said something about Jaymie (the person who was supposed to read the note) and German had something more than just friends and Alana didnt sound upset about it. I hope this German guy [b]does not affect[/b] me and Alana. Whenever we hang out she goes to my house and we watch movies together. She seems [u]really[/u] [i]friendly[/i], we [color=magenta]cuddle[/color] and just sweet talk to each other. In school shes a bit more distant but i think its because she doesnt want[i] Derek[/i] to see us and think the worst ([color=gray]even if they broke up[/color]) Supposedly she doesnt want to be with anyone because of family problems....her brother is [b][color=red]psycho[/color][/b] and doesnt want anyone getting with her. He calls her a slut.....he has hit her before and hes a huge man, hes about [color=black]6'6"" and 300 pounds[/color].....yeah he would [u]destroy[/u] me. We write 