5.0,"[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/allposters/153/1112880_rt.jpg[/img]
 I really didn't know what to expect when I went to see it. Admittedly, I didn't want to see this at all, but I succumb to the Oscar hype. What was it all about? Well, i had to find out. 
   
 The first thing you really notice about the movie is how spectacular the script writing is. Its clever, its witty, insightful, and it moves along. Perhaps the most enjoyable part of the movie is the dialogue between Clint Eastwood's character and Morgan Freeman's. Their banter and chemistry is fabulous. 
   
   I've always been skeptical of Hilary Swank. I never saw [i]Boys Don't Cry[/i], but I did see The Core, and that was disastrous. After seeing [i]Million Dollar Baby[/i], there is little doubt that she absolutely deserved the Oscar (sorry Annette Benning). She turns in sparkling performance, perfectly balanced by Clint's and Morgan's.
   
 The last half hour of the movie was the most difficult 30 minutes of film to sit through - not in a negative way, but in a way that hurts the very central system of your body. You see what's unravelling and it hurts. It just hurts. Clint Eastwood, while not having a necessarily great performance throughout the movie, absolutely [b]OWNED [/b]this period. He feel for him. You hurt with him. I won't give away the ending, but make sure you've got your tissues. And prepare for the pain. Its a very different pain than that experienced during Passion of the Christ, and its very much more enjoyable. What a movie. Whew! Maybe its time to see [i]The Aviator...[/i]
   
   [b]Quote of the Movie: [/b][color=Yellow]""Always protect yourself. Always.""[/color]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-03-01","","RT","900764078"
5.0,"the last thing i was before i watched this movie is that it would eclipse Spiderman 2 and be my number one of the year. it did exactly that. a simple story of a female boxer with some talent but needs to be refined. the man to do it of course is Clint Eastwood. both him, Swank and Freeman give great performances. Its nice to see the academy award Swank for her subtely as a contrast to Theron's over the top performance last year. The movie had me cracking up at the beginning and crying at the end, despite being slightly spoiled by some people. i usually consider myself a moderate with conservative leanings, but the issue that MDB brings up i hardly disagree with the right. as of now i'm saying the acedmy got it right.  but i haven't seen the aviator yet which is next on my list to see.  MO CUISHLE.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-03-02","","RT","900612371"
5.0,"[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/custom/96/10004696.jpg[/img]   I picked this film to beat Aviator for the oscar and damn if I wasn't right on! I so enjoyed seeing this movie because I knew this was a passion for all the actors involved. You could just sense it in every scene. It came across so strongly that those two hours in that theater were magical. When you no longer care who you are and time stands still - that is movie magic! In my lowly opinion - all the oscars were deserved. Although I would have liked to see Clint get best actor, at least he got best director. I will forever love each and every movie that portrays the underdog and down and out trying so hard to reach that thing they are so passionate about. They are willing to give up everything for that one chance. I wish I had that kind of passion in my life - don't we all? 
 
