I liked The Aviator very much and even picked Cate Blanchett for the oscar. This was a beautifully done epic, period piece about a part of a man's life. Interesting - indeed. Colorful, insightful and a joy to watch. Cate was so on as Hepburn that when I closed my eyes, her performance gave me goosebumps! Leo and the rest of the cast - superb. Scorsese - a genius again. What this picture lacked was the ability to pull my heart out of my chest and squeeze it. Howard Hughes is understandably a heck of a guy and has his spot in aeronautic and social history, but..... it was just an interesting three hours in a theater and I didn't cry once! Million Dollar Baby WAS the better film!!","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-03-02","","RT","900681150"
