5.0,"[font=Tahoma][size=2][font=Palatino Linotype]If you are to see only one movie this year, be it Clint Eastwood's [color=navy][b]""Million Dollar Baby""[/b][/color]. This is the best american movie of 2004.[/font][/size][/font]
 
[size=2][font=Palatino Linotype][size=2]Not unlike what he did in [/size]""MysticRiver"", Eastwood who just turned 70 bites the bullet again: he fostered a familiar genre and transcended it to another level. If you think this is another formula sports movie or the female version of ""Rocky"", well, you don't know Eastwood.[/font][/size]
 
[font=Palatino Linotype][size=2]Hilary Swank stars as Maggie Fitzgerald, a hill-billy aspiring boxer who wants to be trained by Frankie (Clint Eastwood), an aging boxing coach and owner of a run-down gym called the Hit Pit. Frankie is reluctant to train her; he doesn't train girls, he thinks she is too old to start out, and no matter how tough she is ""[i]girly, tough aint enough[/i], he says.[/size][/font]
 
[font=Palatino Linotype][size=2]But after Maggie worns him down with her relentless determination; and after an endless wheedling from Scrap - a one-eyed former fighter who helps run the Hit Pit (played to perfection by Morgan Freeman) , Frankie finally agrees.[/size][/font]

[font=Palatino Linotype][size=2]There is no way I can continue further without revealing the plot so I will say no more except that the third and final act plays like a bucket of ice splashed on your face. And it will resonate on you long after the credit rolls.[/size][/font]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-03-07","","RT","900771497"
