[indent][indent]     [center]A Million Dollar Baby is a movie in a class of its own. It takes you to the place you love and then crushes it to little pieces. This by far is my favorite boxing movie of all time, Its just amazing.
      
 Now for those of you that are into movies with the mind set ""the end is the only thing that matters"" need to just sit back and enjoy the trip there for it is much greater. Clint Eastwoods acting and directing were enjoyable more so his direction than his acting. Hilary Swank and Morgan Freeman however had exellant acting and by far stunned me. This film returns acting to the acters molding into the role rather than the acter uses the same role over and over and keeps finding roles that fits the actor.
      
 Now most of you know this movie is about a female boxer. Well in a little more depth the movie is about a lady who wants to start boxing too late into her life and wants one of the best trainers in the buisness which only wants to trains guys. Other than that the movie is about taking a risk. The entire movie keeps risk taking in the plot. Still some moments have key issues involved and other moments, but I find that its mostly about taking the risk and how the results are dealt with.
      
 How the results are dealt with is interesting all in its own. However in the world of female boxing there are no questions, only yes sir, no crying allowed just toughness, and there can only be one person left standing.
      
  Enjoy the movie for those of you that haven't seen it, and don't think about the ending too hard its really all shown to you.
      
  Until my next review, Joe
      [/center]
