4.0,"Million Dollar Baby is a brilliant movie on so many levels, and yet so thoroughly flawed in others. As a writer when I step back to an objective level I wonder what the hell they were thinking by essentially crushing the momentum that the movie had when they put her in the hospital just over half-way through the movie. Perhaps it's just a faithful adaptation of the book, but it should've been fixed for the screenplay. Even if it was left in intentionally to put us in her shoes so we could feel how it felt to have life come to a screeching halt it still failed ultimately. So, the structure was retarded (beginning in the second half), her characters motivation to give up questionable (if she's such a fighter why is she giving up? her line about fighting to get out of life sounded like a load of baloney to me), and the stereotypes of her extended family were overused and should've been written with more insight. However, it's a testament to the brilliance that everything else in the movie is that I still loved the movie as much as I did. Clint just gets better and better as he ages.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2005-03-11","","RT","900771920"
