[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/million_dollar_baby/_group_photos/clint_eastwood6.jpg[/img]
 
 
[font=Garamond][size=3]After Mystic River, I had low expectations for this one. I am happy I saw this movie. Spectacular, emotional, cutting. The camerawork is majestic and haunting; every shot accentuates the mood, the overall dreariness, and the struggles each character goes through. [/size][/font]
 
[font=Garamond][size=3]This film was (and is) deserving of every award it received. Swank shines; Clint is emotionally relatable and complex; and Freeman's narrative, as always, is perfect. I will not spoil it by describing the film any further; I'm not a dick like other critics who feel the need to ruin the movie because they don't agree with it or like it. But it is a spectacular picture of a woman's fight to succeed; a man's attempt to reconcile and live with his past and the present; and another man past his prime, trying to make sure everyone else does what is right.[/size][/font]
 
 
