3.5,"I saw this movie after it had won all the Oscars and I can definitely see why it won Best Picture.  It was a beautiful piece of work, and all the actors were absolutely remarkable.  However. it was the most depressing movie I've ever seen.  As Mad TV sums it up: ""Clint Eastwood's goal was to make the most depressing movie of 2005"".  I wholeheartedly agree with that statement. 

Morgan Freeman and Clint were very good, but Hilary Swank carried the film.  I know everyone is all ""She's not that remarkable, it can't have been a very big stretch for her"", but pretending you are paralyzed from the waist down and wanting so very badly to die... yeah that's hard to do.  And she did it.  At the end of the movie I couldn't even cry, I was shaking so badly.  I didn't get any sleep for two nights just thinking about this movie.  Whenever I hear the music from the soundtrack I get the chills.

It was a very good movie, but I don't think I'd recommend it, just because I felt horribly shocked and depressed after it, and I'm too nice a person to want anyone else to feel like that.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2005-03-13","","RT","900772078"
