5.0,"I meant to see this movie much sooner. And I certainly didn't think that I'd be waiting until it won Best Picture at the Academy Awards. I remember seeing the previews thinking that the movie could be well-received by the general public. I thought it was going to be an inspirational female boxing story with great references to the Rocky movies. I thought -- been there, seen that, felt that. [i]Next.[/i]
 
I was wrong. This movie is much more than I thought. The movie-making business hasn't exactly left a serious impression in my thoughts as of late. I've been enterprised with funny, action-packed, or melodramatic scenes which are sometimes quite reaching. But there's a level of humanity in this particular film that truly supercedes well and above much of the modern movies made today. Perhaps, it was due to the magical touch of experienced Clint Eastwood who's made some of the best movies of our time.
 
They make Hilary Swank look washed out, rugged, and as ugly as possible. It's no wonder that Hilary Swank got an Oscar for her performance. Hollywood seems to reward the ladies that try their best to tone down their beauty for the movies. Weird, ain't it?","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-04-02","","RT","900744843"
