2.5,"[b]Where:[/b] AMC Kanata
[b]Genres:[/b] Dramas, Boxing, Theatrical Release

One line review: Not worth seeing.

Ok, I'll be the first to admit I made a *huge* mistake seeing Crash on saturday and then Million Dollar Baby on sunday. Although, that was the order in which Paul Haggis made the films. Million Dollar Baby can be summed up as another victim of the hype machine. Stop reading here unless you want to read some spoilers.

[b]*** SPOILERS ***[/b]

I have to say I'm probably more disappointed then you are that M$B didn't live up to the hype. It almost did. I think I really really enjoyed about 3/4 of the movie. But ""it doesn't matter what you do, all will be forgiven if you wow them in the end"" cuts both ways. It doesn't matter how good the film was if the ending is disappointing. I was really enjoying the modern day Rocky film when it changes gears and becomes a different kind of movie. I even liked that, if only they had made the end faster.

What got to me about the movie was how after a surprise out of left field, there was an obvious conclusion to where this was going and it took us FOREVER to get there. I also think there was an entire backstory between Eastwood and his daughter that was unfortunately ignored that might have given some greater depth to the plight of his character in the last quarter of the film. If they'd shaved off half an hour at the end then they would have had a sudden, tragic ending to an amazing film that would have left everyone leaving the theatre a little numb and heartbroken, instead we leave the theatre bored.

