4.5,"Well I watched M$B in the hotel room. It was fantastic. I wish I had been able to see it in theatres though. Seeing it in a hotel room, somehow made it lose it's power just a little bit. I was watching it with relatives, and during the end, my Mom was teasing my dog and everyone was laughing. Me and my two cousins were the only one's not laughing. It was a brilliant film though.
 
 
I had a nice time in Regina, I got to see relatives I don't often get to see. My Great Aunt's 90th birthday party was a bore (when are any 90th birthday parties fun?). It was just a bunch of people, most of which I didn't know talking at different tables for two hours. Me and one of my cousins were talking about my high school problems and making fun of Hilary Duff during a lot of it. The swimming was really nice though, there was a water slide and the pool wasn't cold at all. The two-way, six hour car drive wasn't bad though. I spent all my time both ways listening to music and zoning out. 
 
 
Now here is some great irony: while on the way back home, I saw a Mcdonald's sign in a field. Around the sign were a bunch of grazing cows. I found it so hilarious because one day those cows will probably become Mcdonald's hamburgers.
 
 
Am I the only one that see's the humour in that?","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2005-06-06","","RT","900655007"
