5.0,"[font=Arial]This is a great movie! Hillary Swank is superb and should win the Oscar hands down. Clint Eastwood has become one of the finest American directors ever.[/font]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-07-12","","RT","900760104"
5.0,"What is there to say?
   
 I have come to adore and bow before Eastwood (directed) films for their simplicity and yet depth and realism. Nothing however prepared any of us for the turn he gave this film. 
   
 I have never left the cinema more depressed and still upbeat about having witnessed something we have wanted from cinematography for so long: A realistic ending far, far away from those Hollywood-sugarsweet endings (seen War of the Worlds? That's what I'm talking about...).
   
 As hard as it was to witness all that and even though I admit enjoying films to end positive because my stressed mind needs some caressing every once in awhile, I still believe that some films HAVE to be ending like this one. Even if it was just for us to see that art also reflects reality and is not a simple cash-cow drugging moviegoers for two hours into believing everything is possible and the world will forever be ok as long as the hero returns home safely...
   
 Thanks, Mr. Eastwood. Although this was a hard pill to swallow, it sometimes needs a kick like that to be aware of the real beauty in life. And that could never be accomplished by the typical Hollywood thing.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-07-13","","RT","900762702"
