5.0,"This is simply one of the overall best movies I have seen. I'd never call myself a big boxing-movie buff, so when I sat down to watch this movie, I woundered if I would find it interesting. I'd heard it was really good, but sports-related movies in general loose my attention if they aren't really, really good.
 
Well this movie is really, really good. The story may be about boxing, but it is not exclusive to the ''boxing-movie"" demographic (if there is one). The story is a very human story that is expertly crafted by Clint Eastwood so that every line and scene has a purpose and the entire film carries a strong moral message. It's also surprisingly poignant and silently touching as it explores it's theme: which is the meaning of true love, commitment, and happiness. 
 
This is a must-see for anyone who appreciates the true, unabridged meaning of a GOOD motion picture.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-07-19","","RT","900700941"
3.5,"If you're in a good mood, you might want to pass on seeing this, if you're in a bad mood DEFINITELY skip it.
 
 Slow start as far as any real action, but it's needed to develop the characters and it pays off later  in the movie.  
    A little something for everyone, women empowered, realizing your dreams, dealing with family and dealing with your past.   What appears on the surface to be a simply story of a girl with a dream turns into a deep, moving film about everything but that dream.  NO big special effects, THANK GOD, When Swank was throwing those punches I actually found myself whincing.  Some characters I loved, many I hated, but they all left me feeling SOMETHING. 
   With too many ""happily ever after"" endings these days it's refreshing to see an honest film, although this addressed, for many of us, our greatest fear. 
    With all the awards it won I was expecting more, but if you want a movie that makes you think and feel.......... give it a try.   Just don't expect to be doing cartwheels when it's over.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2005-07-22","","RT","900794069"
