5.0,"But not anymore
 
I love food. I will eat almost anything at least once, usually twice. More if possible. But I was never a glutton. It seemed my metabolism was capable of handling anything I shoveled down my gullet to appease my apparently insatiable hunger. I was a growin' boy.
 
Was.
 
Then I hit my late 20's and things...slowed down. Not only did my ranch work honed body start to lose tonality in my love handles, but my eating habits took an odd turn. I ate less frequently, but each session was larger.
 
Then I met Velvet Cyberpunk. She is a fantastic cook. I have told her several times, in complete sincerity, that she should open a restaurant. It was a surprise to me around 3 months ago, then, to learn that I had eaten an honest to goodness home cooked meal almost every single night since last September.
 
Perhaps my body was just adapting to well to her habit of making food that was not only delicious, but healthy as well. Perhaps my age has something to do with it...I don't know for sure. But I will say this - I cannot eat most fast food crap anymore.
 
Not for lack of wanting, mind you. I have thrice in the last month eaten from a burger joint of some type, and each time my stomach has sent some nastygrams to my bowels expressing displeasure. During a quick lunch from Jack-in-the-Box a week and a half ago, I was stunned when I realized I was getting nauseous from the small greaseburger I was downing. I didn't finish it, spitting into the toilet the last two bites I had been hesitantly chewing for the last 3 minutes as I tried to decypher the strange feelings in my belly.
 
Then again, tonight. Another burger, another irritated stomach.
 
What the hell is happening to me? I used to be able to eat bug spray without any consequence, but these days merely smelling a McDonald's patty makes me want to toss my cookies.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-07-23","","RT","900662818"
5.0,"Fantastic and refreshing,goes against the plethora of typical hollywood churn.
 Hillary Swank plays the best female role i have seen in years,Morgan Freeman is his usual downbeat but superb self and Clint Eastwood has really pulled the rabbit out of the hat here with a stark emotional rollercoaster that is as enjoyable as it is depressing.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-07-24","","RT","900796381"
4.5,"[size=3][font=Comic Sans MS]As near perfect as any movie I've seen in awhile.  Morgan Freeman, Clint Eastwood, and Hillary Swank are a delight to watch alone or any combination of the three.  The fight scenes are the only thing that maybe could of been done better but still gave just the right amount of violence and action.  Its a struggle to write these sometimes without saying anything about the storyline for those who haven't seen it or read any of the spoilers.  The story pulls you in and keeps a hold on you from the beginning to end.  Once is not enough, I am a fiend for this movie.  I'll put it on the shelf next to the ""Godfather"" series, the original ""Star Wars"" series, and ""Leaving Las Vegas"".  Just pick it up and buy its a guaranteed lock.  Hell I may just watch it again tonight.   [/font][/size]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2005-07-25","","RT","900790698"
5.0,"[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/million_dollar_baby/hilary_swank/baby4.jpg[/img]Although I love and hoped Eternal Sunshine would be up for more Oscars Million Dollar Baby showed me how A boxing movie wins best picture. First you need Clint Eastwood. And then on from there. Clint's directing is wicked. If I can use that word. Touches of darkness surround many scenes in this movie. Which is the wicked part. His acting is also spectacular. And Hilary Swank is the other piece of the puzzle. Morgan Freeman was just an extra bonus prize. This movie won the title fight, and 4 Oscars this year. I loved this one.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-07-26","","RT","900732110"
5.0,"This was probably the best movie of the year hands down and maybe Clint Eastwood's best acting and directing.The story is entertaing and engaging to keep you glued to the screen until the end, The acting is top notch with Morgan Freeman and Hilary Swank both derserving their golden statues, and characthers that you feel for and love so much you feel like you're there with them or that you know or want to know them. It's also a excellent screenplay along side from everything else thats also great in this movie. There is nothing bad in this movie, im serious. I love my underdog stories and this is a great one of those. A pure masterpeice of filmaking, pitch perfect in every aspect of good filmaking, not to be missed. Im sure you wont be dissapointed....if you are... you're not a movie lover whatsoever.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-07-28","","RT","900783080"
4.5,"[font=Courier New]MILLION DOLLAR BABY[/font]
[font=Courier New]RATING: 9/10 :fresh: [/font]
[font=Courier New]-------------------[/font]
[font=Courier New]PLOT: [/font]
[font=Courier New]""Million Dollar Baby"" is the amazing story of a female boxer, Maggie Fitzgerald (Hilary Swank), and how she inspired an old trainer, Frankie Dunn (Clint Eastwood), to come back into his training. Sorry, I can't really reveal much more of the story without giving anything about the movie away.[/font]
[font=Courier New][/font] 
[font=Courier New]REVIEW: [/font]
[font=Courier New]First off, can someone please leave me a comment and kindly tell me where the title ""Million Dollar Baby"" fits into the movie because that is the one thing that I cannot determine by myself.[/font]
[font=Courier New]This is Clint Eastwood's latest directorial performance, almost immediately after his last film, ""Mystic River"", which was critically acclaimed. I personally did not care for ""Mystic River"" because it seemed like Clint Eastwood went out of his way to make the ending depressing. I don't mind a depressing ending and in fact, sometimes I prefer one because it's refreshing but in ""Mystic River"", the sadness just becomes overkill and a lot of it at that.[/font]
[font=Courier New]So as you can see, I was extremely skeptical about watching ""Million Dollar Baby"", expecting it to follow in ""Mystic River""'s footsteps and have a absolutely terrible ending. I was proved wrong in my skepticism as this wonderful movie drew me in and didn't let me go til the end.[/font]
[font=Courier New]The screenplay of ""Million Dollar Baby"" is proportionate to every screenplay ever written like Michelangelo's painting 'Son Of Man' compares to every painting or sculpture ever created. It just seems to have a divine touch on it and every line is incredibly memorable. Not since ""Pulp Fiction"" have I witnessed a screenplay this good.[/font]
[font=Courier New]But what is a screenplay without actors to perform it? Fear not, readers, for this movie doesn't fail her either. I have always been a fan of Clint Eastwood and Morgan Freeman (the latter happens to be one of my personal favorites anyways) and knew that they would bring life into the movie. Little did I realize how Hilary Swank would completely appear to be a goddess among mere mortals in her portrayal of the character she played. Never once does she even begin to seem out of character and even when she just hits the punching bag and doesn't speak, such amazing emotion still shines through with every hit the bag takes.[/font]
[font=Courier New]My only complaint with the movie is that about an hour and a half into the film, it seems to slow down to a crawl but after thirty minutes of doing so, it picks up again.[/font]
[font=Courier New][/font] 
[font=Courier New]MEMORABLE QUOTE:[/font]
[font=Courier New]""If there's magic in boxing, it's the magic of fighting battles beyond endurance, beyond cracked ribs, ruptured kidneys and detached retinas. It's the magic of risking everything for a dream that nobody sees but you.""
-Eddie Dupris (Morgan Freeman)[/font]
[font=Courier New][/font] 
[font=Courier New]MEMORABLE SCENE:[/font]
[font=Courier New]The last ten minutes but I don't want to give anything away so I won't spoil it for you but just to let you know, you won't ever forget it.[/font]
[font=Courier New][/font] 
[font=Courier New]BOTTOM LINE:[/font]
[font=Courier New]Overall, I can see why it won Best Picture at the Academy Awards last year and for the first time since ""The Lord Of The Rings: Return Of The King"" won Best Picture, I can actually agree with who was chosen as the winner.[/font]
[font=Courier New][/font] 
[font=Courier New]BUY/RENT/LEAVE IT ALONE:[/font]
[font=Courier New]Buy if you don't mind not getting a picture-perfect ending with your movies but if you do, just rent it.[/font]
[font=Courier New][/font]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2005-07-28","","RT","900791646"
4.5,"[b][img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/dreamworks_skg/the_island/theisland_releaseposter.jpg[/img][/b]
[b]The Island[/b]
Looking at the box office, The Island is one of the most underrated movies in history. This movie is fantastic. Right from the word go, you are hooked. The always obvious/over-the-top/slow foundations of this movie are incredible to the watch. The sets are absoluetly fantastic.
 
The Island focuses on a young male, Lincoln 6 Echo (Ewan McGregor), who begins to question his surroundings in an underground facility. I don't want to give too much away, but it is a fantastic ride.
 
The fact that the movie has included technology that we use today and put a 2019 focus on it is fantastic. I was in awe in this film. The acting is pretty good. Scarlet Johansson is incredible to watch. Ewan McGregor in a slightly better role than the crap he was given in Star Wars.
 
There are some very funny lines throughout the movie. But the action is superb albiet a-little-too-much-and-unbelievable.
 
However, the ending is still a problem. It felt like I was watching a Qantas commercial, and it was quickly resolved and predictable.
 
But this is a very fine movie. See it before it leaves. 
 
[b][img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/sony_pictures_classics/layer_cake/layercake_releaseposter.jpg[/img][/b]
[b]Layer Cake[/b]
Layer Cake is the latest British mob-action movie. And it is pretty average. The performances are great but the story and characters are stupid. The much talked about Matthew Vaughn directing (one of the directors originally signed on to do X-Men 3) is actually very ordinary and I found it annoying at times.
 
I was not a huge fan of 'Lock Stock...' or 'Snatch' but I thought they still had some character that Layer Cake lacked.
 
Wait for DVD, die hard fans only.
 
[b]Little Black Book (DVD review)[/b]
I must say, when my girlfriend saw this title on the DVD shelf at Blockbuster, I shook my head. But I have to admit, this is one quiet crowd-pleaser. The story is very stupid, but the perfomances of Brittany Murphy and Holly Hunter make this a great movie to watch.
 
The film falls tragically for that sentimental crap but its the ending that gives this movie some great credibility. The ending is unexpected and could be a tear jerker if you care enough (but I didn't).
 
The supporting actors aren't very good, the very stereotypical sort of thing. But its really Murphy and Hunter that make this movie what it is.
 
Highly recommended. Don't fear this chick flick.
 
Great extras too!
 
[b]Million Dollar Baby (DVD review) - Mini review[/b]
The movie that Hilary Swank won an Oscar for, and she deserves it. A brutal story, about a female boxer.
 
Like Mystic River, this is a really sentimental film that your heart follows right towards the teary end. This film is best viewed with no distractions and possibly seeing this by yourself would give it more impact.
 
Strongly recommended to buy this great movie.
 
Great extras on a 2nd disc.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2005-07-31","","RT","900745524"
