1.5,"Just saw Million Dollar Baby. For the first 45 minutes it was a fine fine boxing film. I thought the relationship between Swank and Eastwood was phenomenal and moving and the relationship between Eastwood and Freeman even more so. What a great study of the human spirit clashing with a life full of regrets and fears.
 
When Danger got roped into the ring, I knew the film was taking a dark turn and I welcomed it. This is going to be Rocky times ten, I thought to myself. A gripping darkness that forces Eastwood to really struggle with the skeletons in his closet.
 
Uhm, nope. Failure. As much as I wish I could just ruin the ending for you so you wouldn't waste your time, I won't. What I will say is that the film goes from character/relationship study to a liberal propaganda piece. The emotions and struggle give way to cartoonish nonsense. Swank's family comes to visit her and oh my God...ok, they're lame and hateful and should die. We get that. But it's handed to you on a silver platter with a giant sign that says ""Selfish Trailer Park Family"". The mom might as well have had a ""Hello My Name is Horrible Welfare Mom"" sticker.
 
Eastwood forgot the movie he was making and instead focused on his political message. Yes we get it. Successful people suddenly and tragically no longer successful might prefer to just not have any of it. Great. I'm not against the ""procedure"" that is being promoted in this film. I'm not. I think in certain circumstances it can be justified and perhaps the best alternative. But it was all too obvious that we had been set up for an hour to swallow this message in the end. 
 
The movie ceased to be Eastwood/Swank and their beautiful relationship and became Eastwood/Liberalism and their beautiful relationship. A movie ABOUT something is fine. A movie PROMOTING something is another. One is entertainment that promotes free thinking and thought. The other is a tool to force the masses to conform.
 
Not only was it overtly political, it wasn't even good. I am convinced the ONLy reason this film was critically acclaimed is because Hollywood loves promoting films that promote its own political bent. If the ending had gone the other direction, this film would have been panned by critics and the Academy.
 
Guaranteed.
 
Matt Clark","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2005-08-08","","RT","900799038"
3.5,"Was Million Dollar Baby ""The Best Motion Picture of the Year? According to the Oscars, yes. I don't think it was, but it was a good movie. Hilary Swank may have given the ""Best Performance by an Actress in a Leading Role"", however. The movie made more than a million dollars and won four Oscars, so it deserves as good of an actress as her.
 
 Directed by Clint Eastwood and written by Paul Haggis, Million Dollar Baby stars Hilary Swank, Morgan Freeman, and Clint Eastwood.  The movie is about Frankie Dunn (Eastwood), a boxing trainer and manager who works at a boxing club run by Eddie Dupris (Freeman). When he loses his best client, Willie, he finds himself with nothing to do but to train Maggie Fitzgerald (Swank), a girl who makes a living waiting tables. She is very poor, and her dream has always been to fight and be able to support her family.
 
 [img]http://www.henrysheehan.com/reviews/mno/million-dollar.jpg[/img]
 
 The movie is a very emotionally involved movie. I really felt for Maggie Fitzgerald like I haven't felt for a character in a movie ever. Her character is a really good person. I really liked her character and was really cheering for her in my mind like I hadn't done for a movie... ever. The other two main characters weren't as fascinating, however. 
 
 I think my attachment, I guess you could say, to Maggie Fitzgerald was because of the amazing actress that was playing her. Hilary Swank was simply amazing. She really gets into the character and portrays her so well, it's touching. Clint Eastwood is good, but not great, in his role and Morgan Freeman is, as always, awesome. But the one that really blew it out of the park was Hilary Swank.
 
 However, the movie had problems. The ending was kind of abrupt and weird. The lighting was so horrible. I don't exactly like watching shadows, Clint. I know it's his style, but it's not a good style, honestly. The other big problem was that the beginning of the movie and the end moved very slowly.
 
 The boxing scenes are well directed and choreographed. This movie is for people who like these kind of movies. Paul Haggis wrote a great script. I was surprised at how much I laughed during the movie, too. It's funny in some parts.
 
 I recommend that people go see this movie if they are willing to endure the slow parts and see that the movie is a good movie with out-of-the-park acting.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2005-08-08","","RT","900761844"
4.5,"Well, I finally saw this film, after much of the hype had died down and could watch it with an open mind...and found that doing that was completely unnecessary.  Looking at it now, it's amazing that it could be viewed as almost three films in one, and I didn't even notice it at the time, as each part was done so well.  
For whatever reason, I was expecting something deadly serious, and was surprised to find myself amused at so many turns.  It is of course anchored by three excellent performances, and none of the conversations or scenes between them ring false.  
I only wish the second scene with Maggie's family had been cut from the film, but the movie is so strong that overall it didn't really matter.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2005-08-09","","RT","900592747"
4.5,"I missed the chance to see this oscar winning film in theatres and decided not to. But it was a good friend of mine that persuaded me to see it. And Im happy he did too.[/color]

[color=black]Before you watch the film, you have to understand that it's not a Rocky-inspired movie about boxing. It's a character-drama thats based inside the world of boxing. We learn about these three characters with their own flaws in life, and how they help enlighten each other's lives. Frankie (Clint) with his ruined relationship with his daughter, Scrap with the end of his boxing career and Maggie with her waiteressing and dysfunctional and abusing family.[/color]

[color=black]I really loved the feel of the movie. Shadows, Simply-lit cinematography and gentle music, both elements help emphasise the intriguing/tragic story. [/color]

[color=black]Clint Eastwood is proving to be a talented director. He managed to expand on this surprisingly simple and straightforward story into a amazing one. Also his performance in here is very touching. Clint is a man of few expressions, but, he can deliver any line (he gets the best one liners) with total conviction.[/color]

[color=black]Hilary Swank is in her best role since 'Boys Don't Cry' as struggling to meet ends meet waiter/Aspiring boxer Maggie. Morgan Freeman is once again delightful as Scrap, giving a strong performance. The Best Supporting Actor was long overdue for him![/color]


[color=black]This small, charming and powerful film is very compelling and deserved all it's Oscar success. 
[/color]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2005-08-09","","RT","900796144"
4.5,"[font=Courier New]There are moments in your life that when the happen, you cant believe you waited so long to do them. Watching [i]Million Dollar Baby[/i] is one of those moments. Ive had the DVD lying around since it came out a while ago, but it wasnt until this past weekend when I finally took the time to watch it.
 
 I was imaging that this film was going to be good, but not great. I couldnt have been more wrong. This movie reaches a level in storytelling I havent seen in a very long time. Each character are well crafted, and all seem to serve a purpose, even if they are on screen for little bits at a time.
 
 And who can deny the awesome flair of Morgan Freeman? Is this guy not the greatest actor out there right now. Even just his voice can make the crappiest of movies ([b]*Cough[i]* [/i][/b][i]War of the Worlds[/i]) seem just a little bit better. His role of Eddie Dupris is a good counter to Eastwoods stern Frankie Dunn.
 
 I am also sorry to say I doubted Hillary Swank would ever do anything as good, or better than her role in [i]Boys Dont Cry[/i]. This movie took that statement and crammed it right back down my throat. Not only does this movie show that she is a great talent, but also one of the best actresses out there right now.
 
 Clint Eastwood shows that he is getting better with age. With a classic like [i]Mystic River[/i] being followed by a film like this, it is impossible to think what he has planned next. Surely, I wouldnt mind seeing it. And this time, I wont take so much time doing so.
 
 I guess to most, this movie seems to be another boxing movie. While there is a lot of boxing in it, I would consider it much more. The movie is more about the people and there interactions with one another. It is about choices we make, and learning a better understanding of ourselves and others.
 
 There are very few movies lately that completely wow me. I wouldnt consider this a classic film as of right now, but give it some time. Maybe I can grow to truly love this film for what it is. Until then, this movie is a definite watch! 
 [/font]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2005-08-10","","RT","900669856"
5.0,"Or not, I guess its up to how your feeling. But I know one scene made me want to hit someone, of course I wouldn't.
 
 I must say, at first I wasn't all that interested in watching this movie. I didn't think it was going to be bad, I just didn't think it was going to be that interesting. I was so wrong. This movie bleeds great directing and sweats talent. It'll knock you out with its brilliant story.
 
 This movies story is more then just a boxing movie, but it doesn't forget its a boxing movie. I'm saying that this movie does a great job of balancing the boxing and non-boxing parts. So if you think you might not like this do to the boxing, you'll most likely be wrong.
 
 The acting in this movie is so good, you wouldn't even know that these people didn't exist. Everyone does such a great job. And the narration by Morgan Freeman is like whenever he does narration, great.
 
 I say watch this movie as soon as you can.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-08-10","","RT","900659855"
