5.0,"A few awesome movies:
 
Million Dollar Baby: An awesome movie starring Hillary Swank as a 30 year old woman with a love for boxing. The movie also includes Clint Eastwood and Morgan Freeman who support and make this movie even better. Directed by Clint Eastwood, who has put out some awesome flicks, like [b]Mystic River[/b]. This movie is outstanding and fills you with strong and powerful emotions.
 
Coach Carter: Samuel L. Jackson is one bad mutha. He is awesome and knows how to bring power into a character and makes this movie GREAT. I am an avid Basketball lover and I enjoyed the ""true story"" aspect of this movie as well as the emotion and power the other characters bring to the movie.
 
Crash: This movie has an All-Star cast that shows the Racism that blacks, whites, hispanics, asians, indians alike go through in a slightly exaggerated but powerful way. ""Crash"" makes its point, and truly makes the viewer contemplate their own life and prejudices that we may have or have experienced, and leaves you wanting to talk about it.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2005-11-17","","RT","900684666"
4.5,"[i][b]The Lost Boys[/b][/i] is one of my favorite vampire movies of all time. I just had to watch it again for the Halloween season. Kiefer Sutherland is really effective as a ""bad boy"" vampire. And who can resist the team of Corey and Corey in their prime. I know a 9 rating is kind of high for this film, but it is a favorite and to rate it lower just didn't feel right. 
 
 [i][b]Million Dollar Baby[/b][/i] was an unexpected gem. I wasn't sure I wanted to watch a film about a woman boxer. But this film was about so much more than just boxing. I was about the relationship between boxer and trainer and how they grew as individuals as well. Morgan Freeman is awesome in everything I have ever seen him in. Clint Eastwood was very convincing in his portrayal of the trainer. Hilary Swank was incredible as the boxer. It was amazing watching her transformation from barely being able to hit the speed bag to being a champion to her ultimate fight in the end. I don't want to give away what happens at the end. Just suffice it to say, I was surprised at the direction the story took and it was rather refreshing in a sad sort of way.
 
 [i][b]Ray[/b][/i] was a very well done biopic of the late, great Ray Charles. I learned many things about his life that I hadn't heard before. Jamie Foxx was incredible in his portrayal. I thought it was both a fitting place to end the movie and an odd place to end the movie in 1979, when his life had another 25 years. But the point in history was a good place to end. If they would have gone all the way to his death, there would have been easily another hour of the movie. Anyway, Foxx did a great job with all the different dramatic elements, the drugs, the women, the music, the discrimination. It is definitely worth a watch.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2005-11-19","","RT","900713000"
