5.0,"Great boxing melodrama by Clint Eastwood. It is phenomenally acted, written and directed. Clint Eastwood has, with this role, buried Dirty Harry for good. His performance is low-key, deep portray of a man who wants to make up his bad deeds, but gets only worse dilemmas for a reward. It is his best work as an actor. Hilary Swank hasn`t changed her appearence as much as he did for ""Boys Don`t Cry"", but her sincereness makes her work here more perfect then her first Academy Award winning role. Morgan Freeman comes little more out of his usual nice-black-old man role and shows a little more of his dark side then usual, only good for his acting. This film has been perfectly written by Paul Haggis and though it is very moving, it never gets manipulative or tearjerking. Arguably Clint Eastwood`s best work as both director and actor and one of the best movies ever made.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-03-10","","RT","900809275"
