4.0,"[center][img]http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d3/Million_Dollar_Baby_poster.jpg[/img][/center]
 
[font=Times New Roman][size=4][color=white]This deserved to win best picture. It was hands down the best of the movies nominated. It wasn't my favorite of the year, but my favorites did not receive nominations. This movie threw me for a loop. For those who have not seen it, I don't want to ruin it, so I'll say this: I didn't expect it. What a powerful movie with a perfectly casted cast and great performances.[/color][/size][/font]
 
 
[left][font=Times New Roman][size=4][color=white]Hats off to Mr. Eastwood for a great directorial effort as well. Not being a fan of Scorsese, I was happy to see Eastwood take home the Best Director honor for this film. Putting all biases aside, though, I think he did deserve it. It often surprises me how good of a director Clint Eastwood is.[/color][/size][/font][/left]","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-04-12","","RT","900763681"
4.5,"Full review to be added later... maybe.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-04-13","","RT","900825756"
5.0,"A movie about violence and ambition that evolves into a movie about love, hard-earned sacrifice, and doing something meaningful with one's life. Grade A entertainment with a beautiful message to boot!This unpleasant and sad theme, in the hands of another director, might have become corny. But the awesome Clint Eastwood deals with such touching story without final redemption, very realistic, making a future unforgettable classic in the genre. The characters and the dramatic situation are perfectly developed, and in the end, the viewer becomes sad, but never depressed.Thoroughly recommended to everyone.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-04-14","","RT","152267471"
