4.5,"A movie about a retired boxing coach who reluctantly trains a ""over-aged"" girl to women's boxing from the outset, but a deeper look at it would show that it is a more a movie about a man coping with his past and gulit from what he has done. Morgan Freeman does the voice-over narrative on it, and as usual gives it a nice fairy-tale feel. For a guy that's played the President of the United States and God himself, he really does have a qualifying voice. 
 
What I liked about this movie is the pacing. It moved quick and never really leaves you time to being doing anything else. The last 20 minutes was a nail-biting, edge-of-your-seat experience. And at the same time, it left me wanting for a nice slice of Lemon Merange (sp?) pie. 
 
I also really liked the dialogue between Clint Eastwood and the Priest. Was one of the those ""great cinematic moments"". 
","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-06-12","","RT","202930248"
