4.0,"Frankie Dunn (Clint Eastwood) is a boxing trainer who is haunted by memories of  ex fighter Eddie Scrap (Morgan Freeman) getting badly beaten with him as a manager. This causes Frankie to lose some very good fighters due to his fear of history repeating it's self. So after a boxer Big Willie leaves him for another promoter it leaves Frankie's career as a boxing trainer in a serious tallspin.
  
  That is.... Until Maggie (Hilary Swank) comes along and wants Frankie to manage her in the womans division. Frankie who is rather old school is rather unaccepting of the idea and turns her down time after time... Finally, with seemingly no other options he decides take Maggie on and sets out to make her the best woman fighter in the division despite her 31 years of age.
  
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  
  
  This is a film that nobody really expected anything from. But it was possibly the best movie of 2005. Yes, It does play with your emotions a times and the film does at first come off as a Rocky clone... But as the movie goes along, we realize this has less to do with a boxing match, and more to do with a relationship between a woman that never really had much and an old man who once failed as a father.
  
  8/10","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-06-19","","RT","900796756"
