[color=#000033][font='Book Antiqua']Hey All,[/font][/color][color=#000033][font='Book Antiqua'][/font][/color]
[color=#000033][font='Book Antiqua']   As usual I was flipping through channels to find something to watch last week when I happened on a film called; ""Million Dollar Baby"". I know a lot of people on RT had given it really great reviews so when I saw that it was on I decided to try it. I thought it was interesting film. I enjoyed this film but probably not as much as the other folks on RT. There are some instances were the characters talked about a certain event (especially towards the end of the film) that wasn't during any part of the film. I'm not sure if it had to do with the editor or if it was a director issue but over all it didn't hinder my viewing experience. LOL! I thought the writing really kept the audiences interest. The actors which included Hilary Swank, Clint Eastwood, and Morgan Freeman did an excellent job. ""Million Dollar Baby"" is about this girl name ""Maggie"" is a poor woman who has very little going for herself other than determination. When she decides she wants to become a boxer she learns to over come a lot of obstacles in order to do that. One of which Maggie has to win over Frankie Dunn just in order to get a membership to the gym she has to train at. In the end they all learn about life. This is an interesting film. It's a very dramatic film. I would definitely suggest this film to any one. Please see what you think.[/font][/color]
[color=#000033][font='Book Antiqua']Fritz ;) [/font][/color]
