3.0,"[center][size=7]Million Dollar Baby[/size][/center]
[center]+[img]http://i32.photobucket.com/albums/d7/Arya20/million_dollar_baby.jpg[/img][/center]
[center] [/center]
[center][font=Tahoma][b]Staring[/b][/font][/center]
[center][font=Tahoma][/font] [/center]
[center][font=Tahoma][b]Hilary Swank[/b][/font][/center]
[center][font=Tahoma][b]Clint Eastwood[/b][/font][/center]
[center][font=Tahoma][b]Morgan Freeman[/b][/font][/center]
[center][font=Tahoma][/font] [/center]
[right][font=Tahoma]Maggie Fitzgerald (Hilary Swank), a poor thirty-one years old waiter from the very lower classes and with a dysfunctional loser family, decides to make a difference through the box. She convinces the experienced hardened box trainer Frankie Dunn (Clint Eastwood) to coach her and be her manager, with the support of his old partner Eddie Scrap-Iron Dupris (Morgan Freeman), who sees her potential as a boxer. Frankie has a problem of relationship with his daughter, and practically adopts Maggie along her career.[/font][/right]
[font=Tahoma][/font][center][img]http://www.cinemacomrapadura.com.br/filmes/imgs/million_dollar_02.jpg[/img] [/center]
[right][font=Tahoma]Memorable Quotes from 
[b]Million Dollar Baby[/b][/font][/right]
[right][b][font=Tahoma][/font][/b] [/right]
[right][font=Tahoma][b]Eddie:[/b] If there's magic in boxing, it's the magic of fighting battles beyond endurance, beyond cracked ribs, ruptured kidneys and detached retinas. It's the magic of risking everything for a dream that nobody sees but you. [/font][/right]
[right][font=Tahoma][/font] [/right]
[center][font=Tahoma][img]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v670/filmpix/scrap.jpg[/img][/font][/center]
[center] [/center]
[right][font=Tahoma][b]Maggie:[/b] Momma, you take Mardell and JD and get home 'fore I tell that lawyer there that you were so worried about your welfare you never signed those house papers like you were supposed to. So anytime I feel like it I can sell that house from under your fat, lazy, hillbilly ass. And if you ever come back, that's exactly what I'll do.[/font][/right]
[right] [/right]
[center][img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/million_dollar_baby/_group_photos/clint_eastwood10.jpg[/img][/center]
[right] [/right]
[right] [font=Tahoma][b]Father Horvak:[/b] What's confusing you this week? 
[b]Frankie:[/b] Oh, it's the same old ""one God-three God"" thing. 
[b]Father Horvak:[/b]  Frankie, most people figure out by kindergarten it's about faith. 
[b]Frankie:[/b]  Is it sort of like Snap Crackle and Pop, all rolled into one big box? 
[b]Father Horvak:[/b] You're standing outside my church, comparing God to Rice Krispies? 
[/font][/right]
[center][font=Tahoma][img]http://www.cinemacomrapadura.com.br/filmes/imgs/million_dollar_03.jpg[/img][/font][/center]
[right] [/right]
[right] [/right]
[right] [/right]
