4.0,"It's hard to say if Clint Eastwood directorial acheivements shouldl one day be uttered in the same breath as contemporaries like Coppola, Scorcese, DePalma, Altman, or even Spielberg. Or perhaps he's a director who has made some solid films that Oscar voters loved.

In the case of 'Million Dollar Baby' I'd have to go with the latter statement. In every aspect it's a solid film, but only aspires to remarkable standards in a few aspects..particuarly in the performance of Hillary Swank and occasionally in Freeman's and Eastwood's  performances though I've seen both do better. 

What Clint Eastwood should be best known for as a director is first for his ability to direct great performances, and secondly for his ability to tell a solid story that could easily be littered with cliches and weighed down by sappy moments or convoluted social messages and still manages to avoid all of the pitfalls a lesser director would not see. In 'Million Dollar Baby' he accomplishes that much, but save the 'great director' accolades  for 'Unforgiven' 'Mystic River' and  maybe 'Flags of Our Fathers.'","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-09-20","","RT","326347010"
