1.5,"[IMG]http://thecia.com.au/reviews/m/images/million-dollar-baby-poster-0.jpg[/IMG]

This is possibly the most overrated movie ever.  I never had any interest in seeing it.  I knew I would hate it.  I was a little bit curious, but I didn't want to spend the money.  I even wasted a Netflick on it, but sent it back without watching it.  Well, I happened to watch Million Dollar Baby this weekend on HBO (not by my choice).  I'm glad I didn't pay for it.  What an awful, horrible, terrible movie.  I [B]cannot[/B] believe it won a single Oscar.  I lost respect for everyone involved.  I even feel like the Oscars have lost some credibility.  What a sappy piece of liberal garbage.  3/4 of the movie is a tired old cliche story about an underdog overcoming obstacles and against all odds finds a way to triumph.  Blah, blah, blah.  Cliche plot, cliche characters, even cliche advice (that we're supposed to believe to be profound).  The thing that was supposed to make this different was that the boxer was a girl!  ""I don't train girls.""  Ridiculous.  Even that ""females proving themselves proving themselves capable/more capable than males"" story is a cliche.  Swank herself has already done that one years ago (Next Karate Kid).  Even the big shocker in the last quarter of the film fell dead.  After enduring two hours of cheesy, predictable, melodrama, the last thing I wanted to sit through was some tasteless euthanasia propaganda.  As if they hadn't laid it on thick enough, it had to become political.  This movie was a complete waste of my time.  I should have gone with my first instinct.","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2006-11-06","","RT","900908713"
