4.0,"Over-rated.  Personally, I think Clint Eastwood is the biggest Hollywood hack at work today, along with Ron Howard.  Both of these guys have Hollywood and most movie audiences eating out of the palm of their hands, and the films they direct are mediocre at best, often unbearably awful.  But because they are nice guys and long-standing Hollywood royalty, middle America laps up their shit.  Million Dollar Baby is a really good movie, and Eastwood's best since Mystic River, but probably not as good as that one.  The acting is top-notch across the board, and the production quality is outstanding.  Looks like an Academy Award winner at first glance, but it's really not cut of that cloth in my book.  Why?  Story, story, story.  The ending is a downer that most audiences don't want to watch their underdog success story evolve into, at least not unless it's directed by Clint Eastwood or Ron Howard.  My fundamental problem with the film isn't that... it's simply that the screenwriters never decided what they wanted their story to be and so the ending feels tacked on and abrupt.  I don't feel cheated by what happened... I feel cheated by the filmmakers seemingly aiming at the Oscar with an underdeveloped, rather cloying little last-round attempt at cinematic greatness that isn't properly supported by the rest of the story.  If you're going to topple your entire film with a punch-line, at least make sure there's an overarching theme and a relevance that anchors it all in place and provides an honest, emotional truth to it all.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-01-11","","RT","900731756"
