4.0,"Maggie Fitzgerald is too old and too unexperienced, and yet she is well on her way towards becoming a champ.

This is a film about fighting, and it doesn't apply to just the ring, but to life. To go through life fighting, and continue to the very end. Live your life to the full or don't live at all.

This film shows that through it's intensity, it's raw-ness and the emotions it conveys unerringly real. Great acting all round and Eastwoods style really shows through.

I liked how it was unconventional in the sense that she didn't win the championship and that she didn't recover either, that we didn't end up with a happy ending, even though the ending shook me a little. It turns out that the narrator is really writing to Maggie's manager's daughter, that he wasn't talking to us and that this film was wasn't even about Maggie. There are good twists and there are bad twists, but this I am not sure about.","81dcbecb-829e-47f0-876a-70b3744ee36b",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-01-20","","RT","450861906"
