4.0,"[center][size=3][i][color=red][font=Arial][img]http://i2.photobucket.com/albums/y44/insomniacsplague/Movie%20Posters/million_dollar_baby.jpg[/img][/font][/color][/i][/size][/center]
 
[center][i][font=Arial][size=3][url=""http://www.rottentomatoes.com/videodvd/certified_fresh.php""][font=Arial][size=3][color=red][img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/certified_fresh.gif[/img][/color][/size][/font][/url][/size][/font][/i][/center]
 
[center][size=3][i][color=red][font=Arial][img]http://i2.photobucket.com/albums/y44/insomniacsplague/Movie%20Stars/7.jpg[/img][/font][/color][/i][/size][/center]
 
[i][font=Trebuchet MS][color=red][url=""http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0405159/""]Million Dollar Baby[/url][/color][/font][/i][font=Trebuchet MS][color=red] is another solid effort from Academy Award winning director Clint Eastwood and ranks up there with other boxing classics alongside [i]Rocky[/i] and [i]Raging Bull[/i]. Clint Eastwood stars as Frank Dunn, a boxing trainer who has managed some incredible fighters during a lifetime spent in the ring. The most important lesson he teaches is the one that rules life: above all, always protect yourself. In the wake of a painful estrangement from his daughter, Frankie has been unwilling to let himself get close to anyone for a very long time. His only friend, Scrap (played by Morgan Freeman, in an Oscar winning performance), an ex-boxer who looks after Frankie's gym, knows that beneath his gruff exterior is a man who has been seeking, for the past 25 years, the forgiveness that somehow continues to elude him. Then a driven, independent and persistent woman named Maggie Fitzgerald (played well by Hilary Swank) walks into his gym one day and all of that changes. Well not at first, at first Frankie rejects the idea of teaching a girl to box, but Maggie doesnt give up so easily, and with enough stubborn determination finally breaks him down and he agrees to train her. She whips herself into shape and as Frank chisels away the old Maggie, she is quickly transformed into a lean, mean and stunning knockout machine; able to send female fighters to the mat in a single punch in the first round. She works her way up and up (even into a larger weight class) and is still unstoppable, but all of that can change in an instant. [i]Million Dollar Baby[/i] is a great film with plenty of truly moving performances behind its knockout of an emotionally devastating punch. Eastwood, Freeman and Swank all shine  no matter how dark the cinematography is  in this gritty drama about life, hope, love and loss, both in and outside of the ring.[/color][/font]

