4.5,"Clint Eastwood's 'Million Dollar Baby' is undoubtedly one of the greatest films of 2004 - and one of the most worthy to win the Best Picture Oscar. Not since Rocky walked into the ring have I been so impressed with a boxing film! The storytelling was so compelling and well told with brilliant direction from Clint Eastwood (and hence his Oscar). Every shot had me intrigued here. The film tells the story of Frankie Dunn (Eastwood, who also directed and produced) who is an old boxing trainer (and former fighter). Maggie Fitzgerald (Swank) is a 31-year-old woman boxer who wants to box professionally and seeks a trainer. She implores Dunn to take her on, and when he hears of her tragic life he agrees. From there on in, Maggie keeps winning fights and she is eventually given a shot at the title... From there, this stylish drama turns into a powerful, moving, and heart-wrenching picture. 'Million Dollar Baby' is a film that will stay with you for a long time. The flawless performances are some of the finest you will ever see in a Hollywood movie. Not to be missed!","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-06","","RT","84783584"
