4.5,"No sport has been featured at the center of more outstanding films than boxing has, and yet Million Dollar Baby ought not be praised only for being a good sports movie.  It accomplishes so much more through character development and the larger themes that it explores.  A few rather heavy-handed scenes that played as if they had been cropped out of after-school specials that aired during my childhood are all that prevents me from rating this film a perfect score.  Despite those few complaints, I thought the rest of the movie was fantastic, with the three principal actors at the top of their respective games, creating likable, wounded characters that elicit our sympathies with each plight they face.  It wasn't the best film released in 2004, but I cannot argue with Swank and Freeman's Oscar wins.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-11","","RT","54cf3e89-ab81-4610-a380-f3bd0e816d91"
