3.5,"[center][img]http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d3/Million_Dollar_Baby_poster.jpg[/img][/center]
[center] [/center]

[left][size=3][i]Million Dollar Baby [/i]is a gritty, fascinating, and ultimately heartwrenching movie--I can certainly see why it won all of those Oscars. I still don't think it quite deserved Best Picture, I would have preferred if that award went to [i]Finding Neverland[/i] or [i]Hotel Rwanda[/i], but this still was an excellent movie featuring some fantastic performances. Throughout the film you get so attatched to the characters, you feel like you've known them for years, and when things go wrong it's very tragic and sad to watch. An amazing movie, gets two very solid thumbs up from me.[/size][/left]
[left][size=3][/size] [/left]

[center][img]http://i14.tinypic.com/4fvi26c.jpg[/img][/center]
[center] [/center]

[center][b][size=4][color=navy]THE BOTTOM LINE:[/color][/size][/b][/center]
[center][size=3]Raw and powerful--not sure it deserved Best Picture, but [i]Million Dollar Baby [/i]was a phenomenal film with incredible performances nonetheless.[/size][/center]
[center][size=3][/size] [/center]

[center]:fresh: [b][size=5][color=red]8.9/10[/color][/size][/b][/center]
[center][b][size=4][color=darkred]MY GRADE: [size=5]A-[/size][/color][/size][/b][/center]
[center][b][size=5][color=#8b0000][/color][/size][/b] [/center]
[center][b][size=5][color=#8b0000][/color][/size][/b] [/center]
[center][b][size=5][color=#8b0000][/color][/size][/b] [/center]


[center][img]http://i2.photobucket.com/albums/y44/insomniacsplague/Movie%20Posters/glorydvd.jpg[/img][/center]
[center] [/center]

[left][size=3]Another powerful and sad drama starring Morgan Freeman! [i]Glory [/i]was an amazing film, with a surprisingly short running time--it proves that war epics don't have to be 3 hours long to be emotional and intense. This is one of my new favorite war films, and as with most I'm sure I'll love it even more on multiple viewings. Denzel Washington is intense and totally believable, and gives what I think is his best performance yet. The rest of the cast is also good; Matthew Broderick took a while to get used to, but he got the job done. [/size][/left]
[left][size=3][/size] [/left]

[left][size=3]Oh, and as for that big battle scene at the end--wow. That was probably one of the most intense battle scenes ever put on the silver screen, and done without all the CGI. [i]Glory [/i]was a movie that left my jaw hanging open in amazement, Edward Zwick's films never fail to move and amaze me. [/size][/left]
[left][size=3][/size] [/left]

[center][img]http://i13.tinypic.com/330e93t.jpg[/img][/center]
[center] [/center]

[center][b][size=4][color=blue]THE BOTTOM LINE:[/color][/size][/b][/center]
[center][size=3]Wow--an absolutely incredible war epic. A must-see, even for people who aren't fans of the genre.[/size][/center]
[center] [/center]

