4.5,"This movie could have been a contender as one of the greatest ""sports"" movies ever.  Hillary Swank's performance as a downtrodden person with the heart and drive to make a dream come true has raised the bar for any actor who takes on a role as a boxer.  But, then the movie became something more than just a sports movie.  Clint Eastwood does a masterful job of taking you out of one genre, and delivering you to an excellent drama on the human condition.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-04-20","","RT","488924338"
5.0,"This movie was a very touching one.Hilary Swank was excellent portraying that boxer.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-04-20","","RT","339838273"
5.0,"<i>""If there's magic in boxing, it's the magic of risking everything for a dream that nobody sees but you.""</i>

This is a film you don't see very often. It's powerful, moving, inspirational and so heartwrenching that I cried through the whole second half. I didn't watch it for years because I presumed that it was just about boxing - but the boxing actually comes second to the focus on human relationships and experiences. It's emotionally very, very powerful. And although the story is incredibly sad, it manages to keep it's humour throughout - I absolutely loved the screenplay, and that's something that I really admired about the script. I thought it was so well written and that the characters were realised with such clear precision.

It's also beautifully directed by Clint Eastwood - it looks film noir in places, and is generally very artistically done and in-keeping with the tone and mood of the film. The actors all give stellar performances (Clint Eastwood, Hilary Swank and Morgan Freeman were all nominated for an Academy Award, the latter two won) - and I think the pure dedication shown by Swank in terms of preparation for the role was Oscar deserving in itself.

Please watch this film - it deserves to be viewed, and you will take more from it than you gave up to watch it.

