4.5,"<i>""Fly there, drive back...""</i> <p>Boxing films are really not my kind of thing, but then this isn't really a boxing movie at all. Instead it's a film about family - both biological and chosen - and ambition and love. <p>It's reasonably well known that there's a change in the films' direction roughly half-way through, although I managed to dodge finding out what that was and I'm not going to ruin it here for anyone who hasn't seen it. Needless to say, this is an excellent film (though at times very bleak) where each of the three main actors - Hilary Swank, Clint Eastwood and Morgan Freeman - get a chance to shine. Clint Eastwood as director here also makes one of the best films of his career, at the youthful age of 74 - astonishing.","",False,True,False,False,4.5,"2007-04-28","","RT","364189142"
