4.0,"This is the movie that truly made Clint Eastwood the respected director that he is today.  Some might think at first glance that it is just a female version of Rocky.  Those who think that would be extremely wrong.

The story of Maggie and her drive to be a succesful boxer is truly moving.  Her growing relationship (thankfully a non-romantic one) with her trainer, Frankie is one that will make even the strongest man cry.  

Morgan Freeman is outstanding in his supportive role.  He proves yet again, as in Batman Begins, that he is a top notch actor whether in a leading or supporting role.  He can get the job done.

The real message of the movie, which doeesn't come until the movie's end is extremely thought provoking.  Audiences will not even see it coming until it happens.  Even when it does, the father-daughter relationship that is forged between MAggie and Franke is stronger than ever, and as noted earlier, will make even the strongest man cry.  This is truly an outstanding movie, and deserved every award, which it won.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-05-19","philip s","RT","ffcf3604-dd3f-41d2-aaa3-6d03a497d5ba"
