3.5,"Fantastic. As much as Eastwood has turned in some good performances, the fact that he finds himself in the directors chair in his aging years is a good fit. 

The film follows the story of a the broken and bruised Maggie Fitzgerald. She's a women who believes in herself and her abilities, but deep inside desperately wants someone to love and believe in her. And it's that emotion that the film explores with depth, as we watch the relationship grow between Maggie and the closed and protective Frankie Dunn.

The performances are involving and engrossing, and they really serve to bring the story alive. And the story is treated with dignity and respect as it leads the viewer into a emotional rollercoster. 

The film is also strengthened by not being afraid to tackle some tough questions. It truly puts you into the story and causes you to come face to face with it's reality as you watch it unfold. And to do that testifies to Million Dollar Babies underlying strengths.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-05-31","","RT","782095644"
