4.5,"In the past four years or so, Paul Haggis has written just a few screenplays... the catchy thing is- they have been some of the best screenplays in the history of film. I kid you not, every single one of the projects that man has been involved with over the past few years WILL stand the test of time. They are all emotionally bound by wisdom and pain. Million Dollar Baby was  a movie tainted by me before I even had a chance to see it- props, Mom- but now- having grown cinematically and understand a lot more about films than I did when I first saw this, the full gravitational reality exposed here was realized. Every person in this film deserved their respective Oscars, along with the film itself. There is a constant undertone of pain and remorse, but the answers are never fully given... and that, my friends, is the beauty of Mr. Haggis' powerful screenplay.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-02","","RT","782171236"
