2.0,"I normally don't like to say anything that could spoil a movie, but I've got to say: I really think it's a shame that a movie with such an emotional and gripping setup could devolve into a commercial for euthanasia. It was well filmed and well acted. The mood was established well. The music was even okay. On the basis of those things alone, it was actually better than Rocky Balboa, but when I factor in the ending, the message, and the hostility toward the Catholic church (I know people aren't perfect, but when you're making the Church's position the villain in your movie, something's wrong), I can't give this movie more than half of the available points, and since it wasn't just absolutely amazing aside from that, I'm only giving it two. I really should have known better after Mystic River...","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2007-06-02","","RT","782195923"
