5.0,"This is a truly insightful film. Most people try to lable this as another boxing movie. While it has a lot of the boxing movie elements it is not of the sports action genre. It is actually a Drama, and a very probing one at that. I had always had a bad view of euthenazia before I watched this film. I still maintain a conservative view of assisted suicide, but I could see the respect and dignity that was shown when Hillary Swank's character was released from her state. While we should not use euthenasia to escape life, we should not needlessly prolong it either. It was an effective film in showing the world another way to look at a controversial issue. That is why it deserved the Oscar it recieved.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-07","","RT","782753130"
