3.0,"This went from a ""Not Interested"" to a ""I watched our damaged copy and then bought my own edition of the movie on HD-DVD."" Admittedly it was on sale.

For the longest time, I preached that this was one of the movies that was made to win Academy Awards.  I wasn't wrong.  But then I decided to give Clint a chance.  I mean, I loved <i>Letters from Iwo Jima</i> and <i>Play Misty for Me</i> wasn't half bad.  But this one really is a bit of a Lifetime / Hallmark movie.  I mean, look at the elements involved int his movie:  grumpy old guy who can't win teams up with girl just past her prime, but comes from a broken family.  They teach each other life lessons until he has to face the fact that she'll never walk again and has to kill her to save her.  That and Morgan Freeman.  Add him to anything and you have meatloaf soup.

Here's the perks to the movie.  It really is well filmed and Clint has this way with atmosphere that I can't even comprehend.  I think he knows what he has on his hands and really milks the sh*t out of it.  There are ways to make this really campy, over-the-top movie.  While Clint is irrefutably aiming to tug at those heartstrings in some of the most shameless manners possible, he at least reels it in somewhat, balancing white trash families with some ""b*tch got served"" moments.

I really have to comment on the over-the-top evil family.  Yes, I know these people exist.  Heck, I probably know some of them from my twenty-five years of life.  But honestly?  You don't think being paralyzed did enough to win over sympathy?  Really, do you think anyone's really THAT dumb that they said that they would bring her to Disney World if they could?  C'mon.  Also, no one would be pissed about buying them a house.  No one.  If you are good enough to scam welfare for that long, don't you think that you could adapt with a house?    I also have qualms with the religious issues in the movie.  Why bother have him be an angry Catholic if he's just going to ignore that entire aspect in his decision.  I think we were aware that he had a heavy, controversial decision in front of him.  Why did we need to really touch on that storyline?  There's just a lot of heavy-handedness to deal out hap-hazzardly.

The more I'm writing about this movie, the more disappointed I am by it.  Yeah, it's decent and Clint really is a talented director...but good God, thsi shouldn't have been one of the movies that won him an Oscar.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-06-07","","RT","782926901"
