4.5,"clint eastwood is probably the most all rounded man in hollywood.  he's extremely talented and he pulls it off once again in this amazingly powerful film.  Acting is impeccable.  the narration of morgan freeman, who is probably the best when it comes to these types of roles, gives a seriously masterful performance.  Clint was awesome, can't move like the dirty harry days but he still has the swagger and that awesome look in his face when he says fuck you.  Hilary swank was also amazing and for somebody who actually isn't that pretty, this movie really brought out the beauty in her because her character had a great personality with amazing depth.  Screen play done by paul haggis was just incredible and there were scenes where you just held your breath.  I loved how they would focus the camera on one side of the face and make the lighting black out the other half, truly awesome shot. Music was not strong but it never is in clint eastwood's movies.  sometimes, there were funny moments because the dialogue was so awesomely done.  Especially with Danger when he does his little floor crash.  I love a great dialogue that incorporates some smart humour.  plot was just fine even though it is a typical underdog movie.  But the ending is where million dollar baby becomes separated from other underdog movies.  i saw this movie when i was fourteen and i had seen movies where guys would die.  heck my mom sobbed like hell in The Green Mile and i was laughing.  In this movie i laughed sometimes too cause the knockouts looked so hilarious but when the ending came around, i had stopped laughing.  By the time the credits were rolling up, i felt like a brick had hit me on the back of my head.  Never before had I felt so shakenly stunned after seeing a movie.  I remember sitting there so quietly....only because for the first time, a movie had really gone not only to my head, but to my heart.  awesome film clint!","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-09","","RT","782405314"
