5.0,"This movie is written in a way that connects many lines and events to one another, certainly a brilliant screenplay by Paul Haggis. Along with that are actors at the top of their games, and this makes for one knockout movie. 

Everything is just so connected together in this, it is unbelievable. ""My darling, my blood"", ""now I can die, and go to heaven"", ""what my daddy did for axel"", and ""fly there, drive back"" are probably the most significant ones. Then there are many more, such as ""one hundred ten"" that just add layer upon layer, and connection to various other parts of the movie. It seems like literally every line in the movie had a significance or a connection to another one later on, or one said previously, almost so much that is if we were to map out the screenplay of this movie, it would look more like a circle with many diagonal lines going through it, connecting to other lines, and to other parts of the cirlce, rather than how most movie are a straight line with a few tangents branching off.
There is so much (realistic) emotional suffering going on in all the characters, and that suffeing was conveyed extremely well, especially from Clint Eastwood, and Morgan Freeman; their sorrow could be felt even just through the tones of voices they used. The character of Maggie was an incredible demonstration of life values and the story of her life is greatly inspirational. 

This is a perfect movie, and a fantastic achievement as one of the final works from Clint Eastwood","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-10","","RT","784506840"
5.0,"BEST MOVIE, PERIOD(.)","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-10","","RT","784434942"
