5.0,"An amazing film. So filled with spot on human emotion and a simple, but very deep and heartfelt story at its core. I am a huge Scorsese fan and think it is a travesty he's only won one Oscar, but when The Aviator was up against this at the awards in '05, I'm glad this film won and Eastwood won as director. Swank and Freeman more than deserved their Oscars as well.
I've said it before and I'll say it again, the thing I most admire about Eastwood, is he can make a brilliant movie and terrific entertainment, without the need to use CGI or hokey special effects. Relying only on his very seasoned eye as a film maker and his ability to shoot real human drama at its finest.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-17","","RT","785471593"
