5.0,"My favorite Eastwood performance, and my second favorite film Eastwood has directed (behind the unbelievably brilliant Unforgiven).  In the first two acts this film manages to breathe new life into the boxing genre (which was kinda killed again the next year with Cinderella Man) by focusing more on character relationships than the sport itself.  Although we know Dunn is resistant to take Maggie on because of his troubled relationship with his daughter, this point is never explicitly stated or forced upon the audience.  The final act of the film walks the emotional fine line between drama and melodrama, never stepping on the wrong side of that line.  The melancholy piano score from Clint himself puts the finishing touch on this excellent film.","57212038-0e0b-4d2d-abe7-910075eb7c2d",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-26","","RT","783714667"
