1.0,"I felt particular disdain for this movie given that Hilary Swank should NOT have as many Oscars as Meryl Streep. That just hurts me. All that said, Hilary Swank was fine in it. She was great in Boys Don't Cry and by that standard she was mediocre in this. I've seen Morgan Freeman better, and I'm glad he won his Oscar but I'm sad that it's for this. Not a movie to remember him by. But Clint Eastwood? Terrible actor. Just not an interesting role either. And how did he win best director? Oh yes, because Hollywood loves an actor-turned-director. Couldn't they have given it to Scorcese? I haven't even seen The Aviator yet but I'm pretty sure that deserved it more than this did. The script was fine and all (nice line: the one Maggie has about killing her now instead of having doctors slowly take pieces of her away) but man the camera work irritated me. Half the movie was black. Ugh. Whatever. Underwhelmed.

