3.5,"I can damn near guarantee Clint Eastwood will dominate anything he's in. He's like the film god's seal of approval. ""Oh, it has Clint Eastwood in it. It must be good."" Words to live by. Here's the deal. <i>Million Dollar Baby</i> has an awesome cast directed by an awesome director. I've always liked Hilary Swank and it's nice to see her knock some bitches around for the duration of the movie. The ever talented Morgan Freeman and Clint work seamlessly together, just like their characters. Yet, I found I couldn't get into the story as deeply as it wanted me to. Eastwood attempts to pull you into two worlds at the same time: boxing and real life. They constantly conflict with one another. It's strange, I know. Eastwood hardly ""attempts"" anything in film. He just does it, but not this time. I did enjoy it, though this was not Eastwood's finest hour in film.","5f70e7b4-6929-4536-b0c8-b48d6de558e3",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-07-05","","RT","786964687"
4.5,"Anyone who is a fan of Clint Eastwood's gritty yet vivid urban American tales will love this modern masterpiece.  It soares from emotional high to emotional low with razor sharp wareness of its audience.  It's central performances from Eastwood, Swank and Freeman rightly deserved their Oscar nominations and wins.  This film is a must see for anyone who wants to be touched by true humanity.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-07-05","","RT","784892090"
