4.0,"An excellent movie!! Swank deserved the academy award(one of the few pretty woman who can actually act) and Eastwood in his best performance in 12 years. Freeman finally wins an oscar, almost a make up for all the others he could have won.What a movie!! Some things make no sense though. Like giving the title to the person who paralyzed Maggie after the bell. she would have been disqualfied in real life even if the ref didn't see it. they have a boxing commissioner who overviews these things. makes no sense. some other things too, the boxing seems out of a date. a very sad ending and a legitamite look at life at the way it really is. your greatest fears come true. Eastwood and Freeman have great chemistry and their arguments are classics.  A legitamite best picture winner and a great story.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-07-11","","RT","787369775"
4.5,"I didn't cry, but it touched my heart. 
When the film ended, i sat there saying to myself: no, it can't end like this. This is supposed to get all better, like almost every other movie ever produced. But that happy, warm ending wasn't there. Instead of leaving me disappointed, this upset actually increased the film's excellence. So what if there's not a happy ending? Million Dollar Baby is even better that way. It's the perfect, textbook endings endings that make films bland and tasteless. 
The ending of the movie was well done, and closed out the film excellently. It left you saying, no that can't be... And the heart-ache associated with that feeling was very well played-out...
Brilliantly directed, written, composed and produced by Clint Eastwood, the story is unlike any other. It doesn't follow the ""typical movie"" path. But blazes its own... becoming one of the best films of the year.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-07-11","","RT","784697753"
