3.5,"Ok - I had a big problem with the 'stage Irishness' of this film, especially the bits where Clint Eastwood's character quotes from Yeats - in Irish.  Yeats didn't write in Irish, he wrote in English.  That bugged me; it was too much effort, trying to make it seem unnecessarily 'authentic', which only made it seem completely fake.  The performances were okay, though a little overdone at times, and the ending was moving, but predictable.  The 'Macushla' thing really annoyed me, too - it should be spelled 'Mo Chuisle', but anyway!  Morgan Freeman was really good in this, and I did admire the storyline of a woman who everyone thinks is past her best going for her dream with everything she's got.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-07-16","","RT","781928522"
