4.5,"Bottom line: This is one of the best movies to come out of Hollywood in a long time. It's certainly one of the best boxing films ever made. And it may be the best movie Clint Eastwood has made to date.

The story is simple enough, though the startling ending ties your Hollywood-trained expectations into a pretty knot. Don't worry, I won't give it away. Although the film will take you to a place where boxing does become a metaphor for spiritual striving, the script--and more importantly, the acting--keeps you in close contact with the flinty realities of women punching other. This is a gritty, uplifting movie which magically transmutes the suffering of its protaganists into something sublime on the screen. In short, this is pretty damn close to what every serious movie strives to be.

I reserve my 9s and 10s for only the very best films. This is one of them. See it.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-07-28","","RT","900880030"
