5.0,"This film fills your heart with warmth...and then breaks it in half.   A man who has been estranged from his daughter, and a woman who has had her father die, are brought together by one of the most vicious, demanding and heartbreaking sports there is.  Eastwood continues to explore the theme of family, what constitutes one, and how we shape them out of the people we have in our lives, this time focusing on the world of boxing. The three main leads are at the top of their game, working form a near perfect script by Paul Haggis (Writer/Director of Crash) w ho in turn adapted the script from a book of short stores entitled, 'Robe Burns', by FX Toole - it's actually an amalgam of three of the stories, that he convolutes together with technical brilliance","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-08-17","","RT","789431005"
