4.0,"SPOILERS AHEAD: I have to give this flick four stars based on the terrific acting performances by the three primary cast. But I have two big beefs that prevent the film from rising any higher.
1) I couldn't have been the only audience member who was happy to see ""Danger"" getting rocked. I didn't really realize he was officially retarded until after this ""bout,"" but until then I was just annoyed by his character.
2) This is the biggie. The whole ""assisted suicide"" angle seemed very tacked on in my opinion and thus failed to generate an emotional response from me. Maggie was such a fighter before this--willing to wait tables for year after year, willing to nag Frankie and spend hard hours training as a boxer. But when she's hospital-bound, and despite the admirable loyalty of Frankie who kept her company, she's ready to pack it in? And Frankie helps her do it?? I realize the whole angle of Frankie ""letting go"" and learning to stop being overly protective, but I don't think murdering the main character was the best way to make that point.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-08-29","","RT","783015450"
