3.5,"Firstly, I'm speechless.

Clint Eastwood, Hilary Swank, and Morgan Freeman.

Amazing.

Michelle Rodriguez would've been interesting to watch if she played the part, but she declined the offer to star in this movie. A shame, because it turned out to be quite a hit. I can see why. In fact, this is a movie everyone should see at some point in their life. The first long movie during which I didn't care about the time, or want it to end soon. This is a masterpiece; a work of art.


Unfortunate Maggie Fitzgerald seems to have no joy in her life except for boxing. Her family is composed of duds, she has no love in her life, and, at the age of 31, is still working as a waitress while being told she's too old to do the one thing in life that gives her happiness and relief. Frankie Dunn (Clint Eastwood) insists that he doesn't train girls, and doesn't even begin to consider such a notion until Eddie Scrap-Iron Dupris (Morgan Freeman) gives her a push in the right direction, bestowing unto her hope at the same time. She goes on to be an extremely successful female boxer, and ends up enduring even more unfair hardships that come her way. To really appreciate this movie, you have to see it. I can't even describe it.

6.2. Wow.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-09-08","","RT","793008314"
