4.5,"To say that Ol' Clint has had a somewhat erratic directorial career would be a total understatement. When he's bad he's very bad and we end up having to endure shit like The Rookie and Space Cowboys, but when he's on form he's sublime, giving us The Outlaw Josey Wales, Letters From Iwo Jima and Mystic River.
Million Dollar Baby can be counted amongst the latter films comfortably. A  strong, well-crafted drama, mixing equal parts humour, heartbreak and tension and polished off with three oscar winning actors bringing their a-game to the table, Million Dollar Baby rises far above it's potential and delivers a complete cinematic experince  that's lacking in so many films today.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-09-30","","RT","788478236"
4.5,"This movie had 2 emotional arcs for me.  There was the first half where you are led to think that everything will go well, and you feel good, but then you get sucker punched in the solar plexus and fall to the ground in pain.  Then the second arc of the movie has you thinking the worst will happen, and you feel like shit, then it does happen, and it's like someone kicking you while you're down.  It's painful, but deeply visceral and powerful.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-09-30","","RT","793532644"
