4.5,"**Warning**
This review contains spoilers.
**Warning**


I admit that I had a bit of a bias going into this film.  Before I saw it, someone told me that Clint Eastwood hates handicapped people.  I watched the film and I didn't really get that feeling at all.  So, I did some research to find his views for myself.  It turns out that he was sued by a handicapped woman for a handful of ADA violations in a hotel Eastwood owns.  Just before this, the woman had successfully sued another hotel for $20K (her lawyer got $48K) and was asking over $500K for an out of court settlement.

I think this film was really about Eastwood's dislike of people taking advantage of handicapped people.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-10-22","","RT","788622024"
