5.0,"An incredible drama. This is probably Eastwood's  best movie to date (directing and acting), for me at least. I'm glad we never find out exactly why he feels so much guilt, but he's well characterized (kind of a catholic guilt). It's easy to see why he keeps such a distance and why he's so protective, cause he never wants anyone getting hurt, and that's admirable. Morgan Freeman is great as the narrator and supporting character. This is also one of his better films, even though he has so many. When he punches the bully who beats up Danger, there's nothing to say but ""fuck yes!"" Hilary Swank is astounding as well. She's got so much heart and it really shows through. Her character truly is a fighter, and she pulls it off so well. I don't think many other actresses could display the kind of drive and heart she does. She's come an awfully long way since Karate Kid, ha. The boxing scenes are all satisfying, and Swank pulls off the punches she does, always making it look authentic and actually very powerful. The accident scene is painfull, and you just wanna kill that German prostitute boxer bitch. Same as when her family comes to visit. They're so fucking redneck, white-trash hillbillies and they're horrible people who should be shot in the head. Sorry, but they're terrible. I'm so glad Clint did what he did, because I'm pretty pro-euthanasia. The vegetable life is just degrading and bleak. Sure, she laughs and enjoys the company of Clint, but you can bet every other moment was hell, with only hell to look forward to. I don't really feel like adding more. I enjoy this movie a lot, it's a great film, a sad film, and a film everyone should see at least once.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-11-21","","RT","783461185"
