4.5,"There's nothing wrong with this film though it falls short of what it could have been.  While the end is tearjerker, the soiundtrack not memorable, and Morgan Freeman's character a pretty bland stereotype, the struggle of anyone who grows up without self-respect (""she knew she was trash..."") to make something of their own unique talents requires this kind of background.  The way it's presented the story is about any loser who rises to become a winner and then loses to a dirty player just before she achieves her potential.

Face it:  most people who scale the ladder in pro sports do not make it, and the risks they take to reach the top can just as easily turn against them.  Boxing is not as dirty as portrayed in the film, but many boxers do suffer serious permanent injuries.  One look at Muhammad Ali and that's obvious.  And that's the guy who WON his fights - imagine the guys who lost.  

Hilary Swank is fully one and half of the stars in this film.  Clint is good and as a director he can pump out three stars in his sleep, we expect more from him and in this film he gets it - from Swank -but not so much from himself.

The mercy-killing question is handled perfectly in my opinion and the film's flat endorsement of one's ability to choose one's fate makes it stronger in my opinion.  I can't imagine why anyone wouldn't watch a piece of art because it endorsed politics they didn't like. That's just ignorance as a policy.  Clint not shying away from what happens when such a request is refused is one of the very strongest things about this film.  Maggie's determination to end her own life however possible is believable and easy to understand as her entire joy in life has come from her physical power and autonomy.  She has literally nothing else, and it's not possible in my opinion to view the end as a political statement exclusively - it is just another expression of the love between Clint and Swank that turns tragic.  Shakespeare would have had Clint kill himself too, probably.  No problem there.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-11-23","","RT","795510114"
