4.5,"Million Dollar Baby is one of Clint Eastwood Classics.  Rightfully deserving the Oscar.  The chemistry that Eastwood and Freeman bring to the screen from Unforgiven( Eastwood's first classic) is nonparallel to any actor combo.  But be warned if you are not in the mode for a tragedy do not watch it.  However, if you want to watch a tragedy this is the one.  Notice Eastwood's slight touches with lighting and score and how they compliment the story.  Boxing is the spectacle in a movie whose heart and soul lies in father who loses a daughter and find it in Maggie and she finds family with him. Then on top of all this there is a moral dilemma which is not answered but addressed none the less. I originally wrote    ""The only downfall of this almost flawless film is that it gets to dark and  hard to watch at the end."" However, this movie is a tragedy and does perfectly what it sets out to do!","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-12-15","","RT","783876038"
