5.0,"It's a great film about close family relationships, the boxing is really one the side story to this film.  The real meat of it is Clint Eastwood's character takes Hillary Swank's character under his wing to train her, and eventually looks upon her as his own daughte.  What makes the movie even more touching is that Frankie (Eastwood) has an estranged daughter that hasn't spoken to him in years, even though he's made several attempts to contact her.  A past history that the movie never explains, but by not explaining the history, it leaves a lot to the imagination of the audience.  This is a spectactular film!  And may very well be remembered as one of the greatest films of the first decade of the new millenium.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-12-16","","RT","791791533"
