4.0,"Million Dollar Baby is a well constructed film by Clint Eastwood.  It has interesting characters, a good story, and a deep message.  With that being said, I feel like I've seen this film before.  All the pieces to this film have come from somewhere we've seen before.  Everyone does their part well, it's just nothing that new to me.  I've never been a huge fan of Hillary Swank, but for what its worth, she held her own in this role.  Eastwood plays his role well (maybe a little to ""gruffy"").  Morgan Freeman plays his role with such honesty that you never feel like he's really ""acting"".  The story takes a turn a little too early in the film for my tastes, and then the third act seemed a little long.  Finally, did Eastwood's actions in the end truly fit the story?  I'm not sure.  With all my gripes, I can still say that this is a good movie, that is very moving at points and you truly believe the bond between Eastwood and Swank's character.  Also, did Ang Lee's Brokeback Mountain steal the music from this film?  It's eerily similar...","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-01-16","","RT","787703238"
2.0,"One would think that with a title like, Million Dollar Baby, that you'd get a film about a wacky toddler who gets into all kinds of trouble with his ""Richie Rich"" like fortune.  But no.  This film was long, slow, quite, mean spirited, and depressing.  Boo, Mr. Eastwood.  Boo.  (""Boo"" as in thumbs down, not - I'm gonna scare you)","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2008-01-16","","RT","573220113"
