4.5,"Hilary Swank transforms herself, physically and emotionally, as Maggie Fitzgerald, a passionate young woman who has dreams of being a champion boxer. This was Swank's second Oscar-winning role in 5 years, the first being Brandon Teena in 1999's ""Boy's Don't Cry"".  Maggie, a struggling waitress, meets Frankie Dunn (a grizzled Clint Eastwood) who owns a boxing complex, and after wearing him down quite literally, he agrees to manage her. With her iron will and religious training, Maggie becomes that champion boxer, and fulfills her dream ultimately, only to be tragically cut down in her prime by a barbaric opponent. This movie also raised the perennial debate of assisted suicide, as a lifeless, yet conscious, Maggie is euthanized by Frankie at movie's end. A well-acted and filmed movie, also directed by Eastwood, who won his second Best Director Oscar for his effort. Morgan Freeman is wonderful as Clint's sidekick and as Maggie's true lifeline, Eddie, for which he, too, won an Oscar. A must see: A movie with heart, and one that makes you think.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2008-01-28","","RT","794874910"
