5.0,"Sometimes, it takes me quite a while before I get to see a movie friends have recommended, just because it's been ages I've actually been inside a cinema, due to a busy lifestyle. 
And no, I didn't get to see it on DVD either, even though, yes, friends recommended it to me...
Was I expecting it to be a remake of the 1941 Reagan movie?
No, it just passed me by at the time it came out.
But last night, it showed on a national television channel, without intermissions, thanx, and I became enamoured with it. Eastwood and Freeman have always been actors I have much appreciated in the past, but when Clint gets behind the camera, the man behind the star takes on a completely new dimension. So human, so us, if you know what I mean. Million Dollar Baby is a simple story and perhaps that's what makes it so special. And the performance of Hilary Swank, in the able company of two veterans of the movies, has turned from a caterpillar into a butterfly. An actress to keep an eye on in the near future.
As a whole, my feelings after seeing this movie were this: don't stare yourself blind on hard, outer surfaces; underneath there still beats a heart, that needs to be soothed. This is a movie about what makes us human. As long as that is possible, there will always be hope for us. Great movie that I'm going to recommend from now on. And yes: I'll purchase the DVD.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-03-13","","RT","811027988"
