4.0,"This movie is cliched, but so what? If that's true, then we should all try to be quirky people that are afraid of random stuff and put seashells in their hair or something. It's one of only three movies that's ever really moved me. Aside from that, it's  other saving grace is it's acting. The first half of the story is generic, and it's not really that memorable. But it deserved it's win, since it was accesible and thought provoking at the same time. It's also a moral question. I wanted Swank's character to live, but not like the way she was living in the hospital. The fights are not much besides the final one, as they always end in 3 seconds. But it can be fun watching her beat the crap out of the other boxers with one punch. It was enjoyable without being pretentious, like ""there are people living in pain every day. do the right thing. euthanization"", or any political mish mash. To compare to another film, it's a modern version of Rocky, but without the Hollywood ending, since people think Hollywood endings suck now. I iked it, and it's a good old sports film.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-04-16","","RT","901099952"
