2.0,"This movie did not deserve the oscar, and neither did any of its actors. For some reason, i dont know why, but when a movie has a depressing ending, it makes the movie seem better. The recent trend in oscar winning movies perpetuates that stereotype. There is no subtlety in this movie, it comes out and says everything the characters are feeling and what you are supposed to be feeling. ""I dont train girls. Oh wait, now I do."" Can I have a best actor award now? Look at how well i said those lines in my rough deep monotone of a voice. ""Dont let him get you down kid, dont give up, I believe in you."" Wheres my best supporting actor award? Im Morgan fucking Freeman! ""Im a girl, but since im a strong woman with a tough background everyone should have pitty on me. Oh no! A freak accident turned me into a hero."" Can I have an oscar now? Wait, I just directed the single most unorigional movie ever with more sports cliches than even Herm Edwards could think of.Ill be taking my best director oscar any time now. Even with doing no origional work, i was still able to fool the academy into thinking this was a better movie than the Aviator! You know why? Because im Clint motherfucking Eastwood!!! Name me two people not named Leonardo that directed or starred in that movie. Thats what I though, because im Clint motherfucking Eastwood and my reputation makes the favorite before anyone even sees my movies! Up yours to all the better movies/directors/actors/actresses in other movies this year! Because weve got Morgan fucking Freeman, Hillary fucking Swank, and Clint motherfucking Eastwood!! Mwahahahahahah!!!!!!!

But sreiously, this movie sucked.","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2008-05-11","","RT","820755557"
