5.0,"Most people I talk to either love or hate this film. They are put off by the ending, but only because it clashes with their political values. This is a tragic love story of the highest order. it is not a comfortable film to watch, but if you are willing to change your idea of what beauty is you will see a triumphantly sad film. This film will cause you to examine what you mean when you say you love somebody. It tool Frankie to show me what it really means: what you do and what you don't do for the one you love. Great allegory for 1 Corinthians 13. This will enhance your understanding of and your understanding of this story will be enhanced by the story of Jephthah in the book of Judges. What I love most about this film is that it took me a while to get it. Definitely Oscar-worthy material on all fronts.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-06-06","","RT","815506624"
