5.0,"I watched two boxing movies back to back. Cinderella Man, and then this. They're two very different versions of the same kind of film, a (melo)drama on boxing. Unlike Howard's trademark nostalgia, there's little gushiness here, rather it feels like a eulogy more than anything. It feels raw, honest, and brutally real.  The cinematography is subtle and only most revealing near the end, and Morgan Freeman and Hillary Swank do dynamite performances. A certain, must see.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-06-26","","RT","791756449"
