4.0,"Whoa.

Swank was wonderful, Eastwood was excellent, Freeman was (as always) fantastic, all the bit players were great: a positively well-acted film on all fronts.

For the most part, the story was indeed excellent, with a few...implausabilities. However, the way it connected to all sorts of emotion through an overwhelmingly depressing tale was phenomenally done. The boxing scenes were also excellent.

Stickler that I am, I have to get off my chest: it's spelt 'mo chuisle', and more often means 'my pulse' than 'my darling'. It's short for 'a chuisle mo chroi', or 'the pulse of my heart'.

(I know, so romantic, eh?)","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-06-27","","RT","788973551"
