4.5,"A directorial success for Clint Eastwood who despite a fairly thin plot (girl meets trainer, trainer says girls can't box, gritty attitude wins trainer over, girl rises through ranks), succeeds in creating two extremely well defined characters struggling against very different adversities and demons that we can all generalise to ourselves to a certain extent. Hillary Swank is superb in her role as Maggie- an escapee of a hillbilly white-trash family, desperate to make her mark on the world and Eastwood successfully portrays an emotionally fraught gym owner and boxing manager, Frank, that I felt added another dimension to my perception of Eastwood's abilities. If you like happy endings, switch off after an hour and watch a Rocky movie.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2008-07-14","","RT","785620699"
