4.0,"This is a film that just sticks with you.  I watched this for the first time in three years the other day, and I knew what to expect this time, but I  still found myself profoundly impacted by what happened on the screen.  I actually enjoyed it more on second viewing, as all the nuanced of three extra years of film viewing found their way to me.  The finish is something that will never get easier to cope with no matter how many times you see this movie.  Eastwood just totally brought the goods here, as this was not a film about boxing.  It was a film about one person's rise and all too sudden fall.  Boxing was just a catalyst to propel the story along.  

Wonderful performances from Sawnk, Eastwood, and Freeman just make this that much more special.  You can definitely see why it won best picture for '04.  Was it best picture of '04?  Well, that's to be debated, but it is definitely an exceptional piece of film making that anyone inspiring to learn about film should definitely take the time to see.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-11-08","","RT","783302115"
