2.0,"Clint Eastwood is certainly one of the great actor/directors of our time, but this Oscar winning opus really doesn't prove it. The first hour is just a stale rehash of the old Rocky formula, with Hillary Swank dull and forgettable in the Stallone role and Morgan Freeman spouting tedious, pseudo-profound Paul Haggis narration over the soundtrack (yet again, Mr. Freeman's considerable talents are wasted in a role where he gets to do nothing more than play the sanctimonious conscious of a confused white guy). Things get even rockier in the second half, when Eastwood portrays the delicate issue of euthanasia with all the subtlety and sensitivity of a sledgehammer. The ending represents a complete betrayal of everything the Hillary Swank character was supposed to stand for, and is just about as manipulative and unpleasant as any I have ever come across. Interestingly, the best thing about the film is Eastwood's starring performance, which shows a grace and maturity the great director couldn't quite muster behind the camera.","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2008-11-13","","RT","831810006"
