5.0,"""If there's magic in boxing, it's the magic of fighting battles beyond endurance, beyond cracked ribs, ruptured kidneys and detached retinas. It's the magic of risking everything for a dream that nobody sees but you""

10/10

Clint Eastwood creates an emotional and hard-hitting drama with excellent performances from it's cast.

Mixing drama which is never overly sentimental and the gruesome realities of boxing, Clint hits another one out of the park.  A tale of worn-down souls who want to see a bit of the days before they gave-up and their hopes which lie on one woman.

Million Dollar Baby is a heartbreaking film which pulls all the punches to knock-out the competition.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-02-19","","RT","850388335"
3.0,"good. just horribly depressing.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2009-02-20","","RT","783863627"
4.5,"<i><b>Beyond his silence, there is a past. Beyond her dreams, there is a feeling. Beyond hope, there is a memory. Beyond their journey, there is a love. </b></i>

A film that anybody can easily absorb. The story was great. It discusses one of the greatest issues of all-time, mercy killing.  It was definitely simple but brilliant. The best boxing movie I've watched. Very realistic. Hillary Swank is a great actress. Morgan Freeman and Clint Eastwood also did a great job. Their performances was very natural. I can't imagine any actors that can replace them. They did carry the whole film from start to finish. This movie deserves to win the Oscar. I like it when simple films win the Oscars. It. It proves that ""simplicity is the ultimate sophistication"".","ec75b515-31e3-416f-b8f2-f5ff04701195",False,True,False,False,4.5,"2009-02-20","","RT","850354032"
4.5,"It used to be one of my favorite. but this time I did not enjoy that much. Anyway, Morgan Freeman remain the greatest actor in the movie. For Clint, I prefer his voice doubled in Italian, cause, you know, his true voice is so feeble. The problem Euthanasia has been solved in a soft way. There is also a religion debate before the action, but the priest does not look very open minded or brilliant.  The American Nation who loves to give a second chance to her sons, is another leitmotiv. And the ones who got lost, are less lost. Boxing is their way out. Regarding Swank, what can I say? She always get awards when she performs near to man roles. She was a girl dressed like a boy (coz she loved girlies) in Boys don t cry, she is a boxer now. Result: two Oscars. She tried to recycle herself playing the role of a gossip girl in the film adaptation of Ahern s novel. But I think she did not succeed that much. Well, as a man I can say that I do not scorn some muscle in a woman. Watching Swank evening dressed I have some spur. Anyway seduction is very very far from the climax of this story. There is some hint to the love Eastwood Hillary, but it seems more alike a father daughter love. In conclusion, considering that Swank played some episode of the series Beverly Hills, I would have really really liked if she had used her strength to smash the nose of: Dylan, Brenda, David, Brandon, Kelly, Donna and Steve","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-02-20","","RT","792021495"
