4.0,"I was surprised of the plot of this film and that is in a positive way. I really thought this film would be the ordinary boxing drama as usual. But Clint Eastwood has managede to direct and(co-star) this film in a way that makes one wonder how he does it. It is not in any comparison with the legendary Rocky, because of the focus in the film is much more on so many other things than boxing than Rocky had. It is a typical boxing-film in some ways, yes, but in others no and when you wacth it you will know what I am talking about. It has many small details and minor characters like the hillbilly ""Danger"" and Morgan Freeman as an retired boxer who pushes Eastwood's character's buttons from time to time.
