5.0,"Everything Clint Eastwood touchs turns to gold. Oscar gold. Mystic River had two wins, so old Clint topped that achievement with his next film, Million Dollar Baby. The surprise Best Picture winner of 2004 (as well as picking up awards for screenwriting, directing and acting) is a beautiful and understated film. What starts as a typical underdog boxing story takes a more tragic and unexpected turn, guareenteed to leave tears in the eyes of even the most macho of viewer. Eastwood's direction and performance are both perfect, the film looks incredible and Paul Haggis' screenplay is touching and poetic. Hilary Swank and Morgan Freeman both won Oscars for their performances (and deservedly so). Freeman is his usual gravelly, reliable self, while Swank is incredible as the spunky underdog. Just a beautiful little film from Clint Eastwood.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-03-13","","RT","798751792"
