2.5,"Wow.  In one word, 'overrated'.  I guess that Eastwood could direct porno, and it would probably be nominated for an academy award.  It's too bad that he didn't, because at least that would have been a little more interesting.  Also, I saw that Morgan Freeman was in the cast, and I couldn't help but remember Unforgiven, and how wonderful that movie was.  Unforgiven this movie isn't, and I can't honestly remember Freeman even being in this film.  Yeah, yeah, yeah, I get it, lots of drama and slow moving tension between Eastwood and Swank's characters, due to the nature of their very complicated relationship.  That progression of slow, slower and nearly stopped character development doesn't really hold your interest for the first 2 hours of the film.  Of course, the acting is fairly good, when not totally mired in immovable melodrama.  The high point for me was the introduction of Swank's character's family.  They set the bar high for anybody else who wants to establish white trash callousness in 2 minutes of movie screen time.  A little too late though.  Personally, I think they would have been better off doing a remake of the Next Karate Kid.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2009-04-05","","RT","803874759"
