5.0,"Arguably Clint Eastwoods best film since Mystic River. Finally a women Rocky. Morgan freeman, Hilary Swank, and Eastwood himself give unforgettable performances in this enchanted and yet dark film about this struggling waitress who wants to be a fighter. Most people would laugh at her, but I had a sense of pity. Watching her was like watching a crippled guy trying to walk. Sad and couragous. This film has many fulfilling moments starting at the first round Knockouts and the near win over fellow champion boxer Billy Blue bear. However tragedy strikes and puts this film in a even darker mood(if its even possible). The ending was controversial, but I thought it was the right way to end it. A women who has no regrets in life and can finally die knowing that she became somebody. If through the entire film, people could only think that killing quadriplegics was a good thing, then they obviously have to check thier pulse. The ending aside, this is an inspiring film that teaches how to pursue a dream.","dff99686-a30c-43e5-acc6-06edb5023347",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-06-25","","RT","901278395"
