5.0,"This is, without a shadow of doubt, Clint Eastwood's best directed film... after Unforgiven. This is one of those films that catches you completely off guard with where it's going. First you get the sense it's going to be another Rocky, but just like that one dirty punch that Maggie recieves, the film gives a similar punch right into the audience's gut and changes the game completely.

Most of the 'true' story of this film is implicit but towards the end it makes sense and it isn't hard to figure out, but the beauty is anyone can watch this and get their own feeling as well understand what it is telling you. For example their was one part that really hit home on a personal level, but I won't spoil it for you but it involves Maggie's family and a lawyer, the rest you'll have to see.

I can put my hand on my heart and easily say this was better than Rocky, in the sense that rather having an underdog story we get a sad truth which can happen to any potential contenders on the boxing circuit. I can also say its just as easily one of the best sports of all time, even better than my recently reviewed The Wrestler. I highly recommend to anyone, not just fans of Clint Eastwood, as this is something they wouldn't want to miss. 10/10","e1f36d74-fa10-4212-a7bb-9dafb4d3c825",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-07-23","","RT","816336340"
