5.0,"Clint Eastwood's tour-de-force boxing masterpiece with heart, soul and plenty of fist. 

Hilary Swank's Oscar was completely and indisputably deserved. Eastwood's directing Oscar was completely and indisputably deserved, and the film's Oscar was completely and indisputably deserved. 

The inspiring first half and the gut-wrenching and touching second half flow seamlessly together to form a film beyond words. Tears and small smiles are what this film gives its audience; and believe me, there are plenty of both. 

Jay Baruchel and Brian F. O'Byrne brought character and spunk to the film's otherwise graceful and weighty performances. Swank and Eastwood stole the screen and flexed their acting chops without any hesitation and Morgan Freeman, an omnipresent part of Hollywood, managed to be a subtle undertone in the film's overall run. 

Overall a Best Picture that needs to be seen no matter what. It is not a bit overrated and is one of the most poignant and stirring films made in the 2000's.","2f1025e1-6aa9-4799-a802-e4ee5ab972e7",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2009-09-09","","RT","812962877"
