4.5,"....with a stellar cast, amazing directing and editing this movie works in a lot of levels despite its stereotypical setting...and with a name such as Clint Eastwood behind the reels you'll know what ride you'll be in once you've started to be in it...
...now, i'm not a big boxing fan that's why i tried to pass the dvd away a lot of times but i guess this time they made the sport a little bit more interesting for me...
                     

                                                                                                 ...the film revolves around Maggie (Hillary Swank) and Dunn (Clint Eastwood) and a little of bit of Scrap (Morgan Freeman) on the side, why does Morgan Freeman always 
at his best when he's the support role?
...Maggie is an overly persevere boxer would-be who wanted Dunn to train him but the latter is uninterested because he doesn't train girls, Scrap comes along and becomes a catalyst on what would become a beautiful relationship, no not that relationship, that transcribes throughout the movie...
...the script has juiced a lot of stuff that you would expect a drama to have but this time it's the right ""juicing"" if there's a word....because the editing and the script is real real good...the photography is well done too...


                                                                                                 ...but sometimes a melodramatic movie as long as this tends to slow down from time to time until at a certain point it would lose a bit of momentum but expect as well that the last 10 to 15 minutes overrides the supposed climax at the middle and becomes the peak of the film until you see the credits rolling...
...i would have to say that all the characters are very very well played, event the tiniest of supporting role is well acted, Lucia Rijker is most compelling as the Blue Bear and Maggie's mom is someone that i wanna kick in the a*s...


                                                                                                 ...you can bet that Million Dollar Baby is drama over drama over drama but it won't get you too saturated because the events fall nicely as the story evolves, there's a little bit of predictability as well and it is its weakest point...
...it's a relief the title is not Mo Cuishle (you'll know) or i would've seen it in a more cheesier perspective lol...","34f13627-57da-4b8b-a789-9db6533b7675",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-09-14","","RT","885582479"
