4.5,"After watching ""Million Dollar Baby"" it's really hard to find something not to like about this movie.  The acting is exceptional, with stellar performances by Clint Eastwood and Morgan Freeman, with an absolutely outstanding job by Hilary Swank in the role of Maggie Fitzgerald, the girl brought up in the trailer parks of middle America who just wants to ""get her shot"" as Freeman accurately puts it.  Eastwood's solid directing makes the plot believable, and while the ending drew its share of controversy, it managed to avoid overshadowing the main points of the story.  While the film asks the viewer to make a few leaps of faith regarding the boxing profession, the ever changing relationship between Eastwood and Swank will make it hard not to be captivated and drawn in.  ""Million Dollar Baby"" will make you think, make you cheer and make you cry. And at the end, you'll be glad you took the time to watch it.","93760468-5f97-44c2-a3f1-84ea23f41755",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-11-04","","RT","901325782"
