5.0,"Clint Eastwood has a hard time in this film, directing, producing and acting a lead role, so it only comes as even more of a surprise to me that not only is this an incredible film, it's the top of the entire sports genre in my opinion, and yes, I have seen both Raging Bull and Rocky. Saying that, it does use the Rocky formula of an underdog rising up to become an absolute legend, but rather than simply copy it and be a pointless rip-off, it takes an interesting approach by handling women's boxing instead of men's. The plot is amazing, well thought out and a great joy to watch. The characters only amplify it, as they all do the jobs they are meant to do flawlessly. You feel the triumphs and the falls, and this film is the first ever to make me cry. The acting from the entire cast is incredible, and you genuinely believe that the characters are real people. The score is great, and the sets are fantastic. The boxing scenes, for the people watching it purely for the sport, are superb. They're intense, believeable and you actually forget that this is a fictional film. It's not quite in my Top 10 favourite films ever, but it's not that far off and is one I will regard highly for years to come.","78e5e09b-5d01-48c9-b2d0-ef8784557338",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-12-27","","RT","901295181"
