5.0,"This is Clint Eastwoods best.  I was going to give it a 90% for whatever reason and then viewed the 2:30 minute trailer and said ""ah heck with it"".  Fantastic movie.  Love how it hits all the right notes for me. I wanted to smack her mom and sister so badly, by design of course. Well,... It worked.  :)
It's dark and kinda grey filming would have to have been purposely done. I don't think he just got lucky. Couple that with the somber piano throughout in the background.  I felt for all the characters.  
Very sad if you are lucky enough to care at all about anyone on the screen. And I am a sucker for a Morgan Freeman narration. (""Like a twinkie. Like a twinkie.""   *For any Family Guy fans out there*)
Just a perfectly cast film and all around really well-acted.","e2955e2e-2287-491b-b168-b13a0f4f50a7",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-01-08","","RT","901358365"
2.0,"I can't understand the fuzz around this movie. It's just so... nothing. What is this movie trying to tell us? That if you try enough and believe in yourself, you can be a woman-boxer? So fucking what. This whole fucking ""women can do anything, watch us do this and that and praise us because we are doing it"" scene is so goddamn annoying I wanna smash my head with a hammer. It's not that I'm some kind of misogynist, but it's because the scene is so annoying. I haven't permitted women from doing anything but women can't just expect us men to praise them all the time because they're able to do same things as men. Just do your thing and shut the hell up about it.

About this whole scene...

It's like someone in Hollywood decided that there must be a fucking global trend of women-boxers around the world and suddenly there was Eva WahlstrÃ¶m here in Finland. Everyone was talking about her all the time. Of course it's nice that we have a good boxer here and it's even nicer that she's a woman. But so what? Of course there had to be a fucking movie about a strong-willed woman who wants to be a boxer. It's like someone's planning these kind of trends beforehands and releasing them around the world whenever seeing it fit enough. Irritating.

About the movie... It was just nothing. The story is your typical Clint Eastwood -directed drama where the protagonist fights for his/her success in life and everything seems to be fucking A until he/she gets shot/smashed in the face eventually dying.

What was the moral in this story? Gran Torino's setting was more interesting than this, although the story was really similar, especially the ending. If GT was trying to say ""It does not matter if you're a bitter old man hating chinese people if you get some young dudes behind the bars and then die"", then MDB is trying to tell us that ""it's admirable to be a woman boxer because if you insist it enough, some old guy is gonna train you and then you die because you were not that good of a boxer after all and because of that you get hit in your face and turn into a fucking vegetable."" 

I can understand why women like this movie and it's because women like to cry. If men like laughing, shooting with guns, drinking alcohol, fucking, smoking dope, farting, telling jokes and watching porn, women like crying. Even if it's not sensible at all, they like crying like hell. Crying is like the ultimate drug for women because it makes chocolate taste better or something strange shit like that. Crying is the justification for this kind of movies to exist. Because it's sad to see a feminine hero eventually die in this kind of movie against all the laws of goodness, it's sad and because of sadness, the crying exists. Of course crying is the most important thing when handling emotions and thus emotions are important and if a movie awakens those emotions it must be fucking good movie.

Wrong.

Million Dollar Baby was just boring. If she had won that final match and partied like Rocky Balboa this would have been a lot better movie. Now it's just a goddamn cry-festival with no real motives. Usually I don't like Hilary Swank almost at all, but she was decent in this one. Clint himself was as usual as he can be. A grumpy old man just grinning his teeth all the time. Morgan Freeman, I've grown to dislike you nowadays. You've been doing that same damn role over and over again. Do something or I'm gonna start bashing you. That smartass old black guy who knows everything beforehands... I'm not buying it anymore.

This is the feminine Rocky movie. It's like some kind of spin-off of Rocky, dubbed ""Rockette"" or something. If Rocky wins a match, he parties like an animal and if he doesn't, he gets up, trains like a fucking lunatic and tries again (and wins and parties like an animal!!!) but Million Dollar Baby (Rockette) just whines and bitches, gets smashed in her face and dies. Wow, what a fucking let-down.

It's not a bad movie, to be honest, but I'm bashing it just because everyone seems to love it like hell even though there's really nothing to celebrate.","92f761da-d757-444c-8655-834fcfe09abe",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2010-01-08","","RT","800656293"
