4.5,"Dare I say, best sports movie ever? If not the best, it definitely is among them. Clint Eastwood has proven time and time again that he is one of the best directors to ever grace the silver screen. And not only for cowboy and detective movies. I honestly believe that he can make any kind of movie that he wants to.

This goes without saying, but if you have seen this movie you know that the performances are all incredible. I wouldn't expect anything less from Morgan Freeman and Mr. Eastwood. I have to admit I never really cared for Hilary Swank, but her performance in this movie definitely deserved the credit it got. You don't have to take my word for it. Besides the movie winning Best Picture in 2004, Hilary Swank won Best Actress and Morgan Freeman won Best Supporting Actor. Clint Eastwood was nominated for Best Actor, but there were so many other great nominees that year, him winning was unlikely.

I haven't had the pleasure of seeing Clint Eastwood's entire body of work, but I'm pretty sure its safe to say that Million Dollar Baby was one of his top three as Director. Great movie.","f67019af-e52e-4532-a1ff-5ad59fb5cb2a",False,True,False,False,4.5,"2010-01-10","","RT","901316707"
4.0,"This movie was what I expected, maybe even a little bit better. It's interesting because on one hand it plays a long with many of the conventions of the genre, but the acting is so strong and the pace is so perfect that it still feels fresh and engaging.

The final act is where it truly ""shines"", even though that is hardly the proper word. It's one of those endings that just leaves you in a pool of depression. The whole world seems black. I have a hard time with this subject anyway, and the movie did a splendid job of knocking me out with it. 

On the big ""controversy"" of Frank's decision - it was by far the right thing to do. If people want to die, and have a pretty darn good reason for wanting to die, they should have that choice. It's nothing even remotely comparable to suicide. It's just wanting to be put out of your misery.

So yeah, it's one of those movies that you can definitely say is great, but find it very hard to watch and probably never rewatch. It has a strong, but dark power.","4d3a7292-65ce-4392-852c-ade9e8f9d350",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-01-10","","RT","900794091"
