5.0,"Clint Eastwood directs, produces, stars, and composes music for this drama. And yes, I said drama. Like ""Rocky"", ""Million Dollar Baby"" is not a ""sports"" movie. It is a full on drama that happens to have sports in it, in this case (like Rocky again) boxing. 

""Million Dollar Baby"" is about an old ""cutman"" named Frankie who spends his days training people in his gym. When Frankie's pupil leaves due to Frankie's reluctance to let him go for the championship, Frankie is left with no one to train. That is until a waitress named Maggie begs him to train her. Although he insists ""I don't train girls"", he eventually gives in. What follows is one of my favorite screen relationships of all time as Maggie goes from just being a poor waitress, to be a half-minute man (or woman) in the ring. 

This film is just wonderful. The cinematography is very dark and full of shadows, but that's just the world that the film wants to put us in. It's about has-beens and hopeless ""trash"" scraping the bottom of the barrel for something they love. 

Clint Eastwood is just as mean as ever...but that's not all there is. He's also very compassionate, which is great to see. Although some would argue that Eastwood's best years were his Western and Dirty Harry years, I beg to differ. Although Harry Calahhan and ""The Man With No Name"" are iconic characters, Eastwoods later years are full of wonderful performances that show off the acting range, and the sentimentality, he has accumulated in his old age. Morgan Freeman is also great in this film, providing stellar narration for a lot of the film as well as giving us a great character. But few would disagree that neither of these characters is the star of the film. No, that my friends goes to Hilary Swank as Maggie. The performance she gives in this film is very natural and very likeable. With this film, she's forgiven for being in movies like ""The Next Karate Kid"". 

I can't recommend this enough. Clint Eastwood's best movie by far.","f3ffa0a3-4a21-4e21-8dfe-5ddc85ffa901",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-03-06","l m","RT","3852e963-75bb-4a9b-838f-6d5250a9d0c5"
