4.5,"This is probably the finest Eastwood work.
When I read the synopsis of this movie i thought "" oh, graet another movie about a poor girl who works as a waitress and then found someone who helps her to follow her dreams "". But then when I saw the movie I realized that Clint Eastwood has the power to turn the most familiar plot into an emotional, imaginative movie filled with great performances.
The story is about a boxing trainer  called Frankie 
( Eastwood ) who has been cast aside by all his relatives. One day a girl called Maggie Fitzgerald ( Hilary Swank )asks him to train her, but he refuses saying that he doesn't train girls. With the help of Frankie's employee ( Morgan Freeman ) she convinces him to train her. And then the movie goes on showing her training, her fights and their relationship. 
In most of Clint's movies you feel excited and not sad, well this happens in this one is probably one of the saddest movies I've seen. The performances are great, in all Eastwood movies you can see that behind that face of "" I1m a pissed of guy, don't mess with me "" there is a sensible person, and this is much more clear in this movie. It's great

It won the Academy Awards for Best Picture, Best Director ( Eastwood ), Best Actress ( Hilary Swank ) and Best Supporting Actor ( Morgan Freeman ). It was also nominated for Best Actor ( Eastwood, lost for Jamie Foxx in Ray ), Best Adapted Screenplay ( lost for Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind ) and Best Editing ( lost for The Aviator ).

Eastwood done it again! It's a grat movie that you're going to love. Final Rating: 8,3/10 meaning Just Amazing.

