3.5,"The first three quarters of Clint Eastwood?s well received movie plot familiar territory ? many of the clichés of the sports film are ploughed, with the director?s own character as an ?eminence grise?, slowly putting to one side his preconceived habits to train the plucky newcomer from the wrong side of the tracks ? a series of whirlwind victories in the ring almost deserving of the fast forward button. At this point, and despite a characteristically charismatic performance from Eastwood himself, one is left feeling one has seen it all before ? ?Rocky Wrestler? territory.

But a wrenching plot twist it would be irresponsible to divulge in a review, even on as unvisited and clunky a website as Flixster, leads the film into a whole new dimension and provocation for a debate on a major social issue of the day. The flinty passion Eastwood shows in his relationship with Swank is beautifully understated and a subplot involving a wannabe boxer with learning disabilities is also very well handled. Morgan Freeman?s character is as likeable as ever although fairly pointless to the whole exercise - I found the voiceover to be predictable and hackneyed. In all, a highly watchable film with moving moments, but ever so slightly over rated.","627abbd8-1c37-4f4a-8680-e398e8dd1741",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2010-03-15","","RT","892352918"
