4.5,"This film seems a long way from the average hollywood movie where happy endings seem to be the norm.  It is a gritty movie that feels true to life and you could quite easily imagine the story unfolding.  It is that ordinariness that is one of the film's greatest strengths in my opinion.  It is a sad and yet hopeful movie at the same time.  The sadness comes when Hilary Swank's character gets badly injured, her family turn out to be horrible and when Clint Eastwood's character turns off her life support machine.  The optimistic aspects of the film came from Eastwood's touching fatherly relationship with Swank after becoming estranged from his own family and the bond between Eastwood's and Freeman's characters.  In addition, it was good to watch Freeman decking the youth that was bullying the young lad who was often at the gym.  Eastwood, Freemnan and Swank all put in great performances and this was/is a fantastic, but poignant movie.","e43bcd39-eb2b-4a19-a5e9-f69c4922f4d6",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-04-16","","RT","901401912"
