5.0,"Let's get one thing clear: this is NOT a movie about boxing. 
It has boxing in it, yes, but this film, another masterpiece from the incomparable Clint Eastwood, is much, much more. It's remarkable--part study of the relationships between people, part coming-of-age story, part underdog story. It's essentially a roller-coaster ride of emotions, and throws in a few surprise punches here and there. Clint Eastwood is Clint Eastwood, and it's perfect here; Hilary Swank and Morgan Freeman turn in incredible performances. Deliberately directed, and touching without being saccharine. If you'll excuse the pun, MILLION DOLLAR BABY is a knockout.","d42555f3-12b6-49b6-82a5-f99322ded082",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-04-25","","RT","833193882"
