4.5,"I'm gonna have to say that this is my favorite Clint Eastwood movie. and it is a total masterpiece. I absolutely LOVED watching it. I feel that this film deserved EVERY award that it got. and boy did it get a lot of Oscars. it collected Oscars such as Best Actress, Best Picture, and Best Director. Morgan Freeman got his due and collected his Oscar statuette as well. If I may be so bold, I will call this movie a masterpiece. i loved how the characters were just ordinary people. I loved how well Eastwood made us sympathize with the characters especially Maggie. I liked the line ""she was trash and she knew it"" it made us sympathize with her character. also, I despised Maggie's mother. absolutely hated her. she deserves to have major bad luck befall her. I mean come on, her daughter buy's her a house and she turns it down because she wants to keep living off of welfare and she then goes on to make fun of how Maggie earns her living. and then if that isn't enough, well, i can't say becasue it would ruin the ending for those who haven't seen it. for those who have, just think of the last time she sees her mother when her mother comes in with the lawyer. ooh that makes me mad. anyway, this movie is perfect in every way. Clint Eastwood has a way of making you like his characters and enjoying his stories immensely. Final Verdict: right on. a perfect film. oh and for those of you who have seen this movie, go to the Top Critics section for this movie and read the full review of Charles Taylor of salon.com. yeesh.

