2.5,"Production budget: $30 million
Box office gross: $217 million
Hollywood tackling euthanasia (the subject that ethics scholars tend to balk at, when faced with its sheer weight) in A BOXING MOVIE: priceless.

I have a theory (yes, again) about Million Dollar Baby. It was supposed to be a feel-good poor-girl-finds-happiness-and-begins-to-believe-in-herself-through-boxing film ... something like The Blind Side, only more gritty and less Sandra Bullock, when  this conversation happened:


Clint Eastwood: ""You know what, Paul, I don't think we have enough conflict here. It all just comes too easy for that girl ... you know what I mean? We need to go deeper than this if we want the Academy to give us that gold-plated britannium trophy that looks like a penis for being The Bestest Movie in This Creative Drought of a Year.""

Paul Haggis: ""I don't know, Clint, it looks OK to me....""

Clint Eastwood: ""You're deceiving yourself, Paul. Just think of what we're up against: a movie about an obsessive compulsive film director - slash - air pilot who goes completely bonkers in the end, AND a movie about a playwright who thinks he's Peter Pan. BOTH TRUE STORIES!"" *pause*  ""We need to up our game, Paul. That's all I'm sayin'.""

Paul Haggis: ""Well, I suppose we can kill the boxer chick in the end....""

Clint Eastwood: ""This is not enough, Paul. N-o-t  e-n-o-u-g-h. I want us to go controversial. What would you say the most controversial issue is?""

Paul Haggis: ""1st and 2nd Amendments to the Constitution that give the freedom of the press to protect their sources of information, provide for the separation of church and state, and cause problems with gun control?""

Clint Eastwood: ""Ahh ... other than that.""

Paul Haggis: ""Abortion? Euthanasia? Immigration policy...?""

Clint Eastwood: ""Yes!""

Paul Haggis: ""What, immigration policy? How is this going to work in our movie? And it's already almost finished anyway, isn't it? Seriously, Clint. I understand that you already have a 2-hour film that depicts like nothing anybody has seen before the drive, determination, resilience ... and it's got HEART! You know, a lonely disillusioned boxing trainer Frankie rediscovers his passion for the sport and finds in his new pupil the daughter he has long ago lost.""

Clint Eastwood: ""No. No, not the immigration policy -- the other one. Euthanasia! We'll get Frankie to euthanize the boxer chick. And just to be really, absolutely 100% sure that we have enough drama, how about we make him Catholic as well? Because I want everybody to understand CLEARLY how difficult this is for Frankie: even if assistance in suicide was not the most enormous and arguably selfish request one human being could make of another, even if he had not come to love her as his own child. I want to throw a conflict of conscience into it as well.""  *takes five minutes to think about it*  ""It won't take much: we'll just stitch our new 10-minute euthanasia ending onto the movie we already have and stick two 3-minute scenes at random points in the film of Frankie discussing God and shit like that with his priest where we'll establish that Frankie attends mass every day, so he must be a proper Catholic.""

Paul Haggis: ""OK, whatever you say, Clint. It's your movie.....""","94eb0dac-ac53-46a8-806d-407ee7417944",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2010-07-14","","RT","901396044"
