3.5,"Is the glass half full, or is it half empty? There should be a category for movies that are exactly half good/half bad. Consider ""Castaway"" with Tom Hanks. The marooned-on-the-island segment was a 5 star tour-de-force, but the cloying, tear-jerking rest of it was terrible. It was half great/half bad. If there was a category for this, ""Million Dollar Baby"" would qualify. 

It starts as an uplifting, gritty sports movie with Hilary Swank, and she is excellent here. I don't want to come off as sexist, but I must confess I wasn't exactly looking forward to a woman's boxing picture. Hell, even foxy-boxing creeps me out a little bit, but Hilary Swank won me over with a touching, determined performance. She's good. (She was great in ""Insomnia"" too. I know this woman has won two Oscars but for some reason I still feel she is underrated. Why is that?) But, alas, this movie eventually devolves into a totally different picture. TOTALLY different. I won't spoil it, but that other movie that has latched itself onto this top-shelf boxing flick...yeah, well, that movie sucks.","3eb6bed6-6b59-4eb9-9ac6-3a6ca6b81d34",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2010-07-22","","RT","901395601"
