4.0,"She sort of had one thing to prove, to herself, and she was done. We don't truly know how we affect others, but we can choose how we relate. The old man is inspired to lose a lot of emotional baggage and fix deep-seated issues. So he has to prove himself too. The ending says we know life can be a pain machine (mental and physical- they are in boxing- ppl seeking punishment and self-esteem), but why prolong it needlessly when there is nothing left to prove. So she needed him to act and he needed to make that decision, to understand what life is. Interesting insights from Clint.","10354b2f-d8f5-49b4-81e9-ec5060396929",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-08-11","","RT","783074517"
