4.5,"Before I watched this film I always assumed that Rocky was the best boxing film ever put together; now I realize that I'm wrong. Million Dollar Baby takes female boxing to new heights, the story of amateur boxer Maggie Fitzgerald is dramatic, emotional, and brutal. Clint Eastwood lends a hand with an incredible performance, and really showcases the climb to the top. Morgan Freeman defined the 'supporting actor' role, while he didn't steal the show he still supported the cast in an incredible fashion. Million Dollar Baby is a must see, I guarantee after you do you'll take back your previous opinion on female boxing.","04842364-f54a-47bc-81e1-73557fab07cb",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-08-19","","RT","901280275"
3.0,"I think Million Dollar Baby is a average movie. I know people think it's a masterpiece but I have to disagree. 
I think Eastwood wasn't at his best and in more recent years he has shone more then he did in this, which all said and done is still a very good movie but not his best. (My option only)
I think Hilary Swank was the star for me and I must say I find her to be a very talented modern day actress.
Maybe I don't love this movie as much because the ending was spoilt by a friend (Thanks for blowing the end bud) 
But taking that into consideration it's still not a five star movie.
I think a 3 star is a fair reflection on the basis of Eastwood's recent work but don't be put off as it is a very good and moving film which has a very uplifting feel about never giving up on your dreams and also that no matter how bad of a person you may or have been you can always find inner redemption by a act of humanity towards another human being.","d34826e8-2e0b-4755-9aa3-f25377c03d18",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2010-08-22","","RT","789115334"
