4.0,"I saw this when it first was available for home viewing and left it on recently when I was doing something else. When I first saw it, I got the Swank performance and the story had enough of a twist and turn underdog story to it. It wasn't until I watched it again that I really got Clint Eastwood's performance. I didn't think he was so great in Gran Torino. This one was such a nuanced performance that it comes across so effortless that you have to wonder how much he thought about his performance over directing - because it sure is a well directed movie. 

I ended up watching this movie again more so than doing what I was doing to start with. Also because I didn't realize Anthony Mackie was in it. While I did hate that it was such a dimly lit movie, I really appreciated what Eastwood did for the performances. People have said that he is one of the best actor's directors today (I throw Arnofsky, Scorsese, Mangold, Nichols and a few others in there too), and I agree. The story doesn't have enough depth in the beginning, but can't complain too much. It's a good movie.","6b1324b2-95eb-40f1-b060-d25b3add8f83",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-11-01","","RT","825174297"
