3.0,"It was so sad to see Maggie complete one obvious purpose of her life, and then give up on finding the next.  The movie ended with a massive emphasis on depression, futility and hopelessness--things the Church is supposed to overcome, but epic failed to do in the film, and probably in the writer's background as well.  Holier-than-thou believers, beware!  You might wind up in one of my films one day!","3a9009e4-5c05-4612-a7d1-3426dd20a956",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2010-11-22","","RT","906076560"
5.0,"Million Dollar Baby is a Masterpiece. Clint Eastwood has brought back the boxing genre to cinema, tho this time around there is a powerful story beyond what I could of imagined. Million Dollar Baby is about an old boxing trainer which is played by Clint Eastwood and his name is (Frankie). (Frankie) has been training this young boxer for Years now and he was training him to get to the World championship, tho unfortunately one day the Boxer turns up to (Frankies) door step to tell him some dissapointing news. Frankie's boxer tells him that he has found a new trainer that would get him to the championship much quicker, so than Frankies boxer leaves Frankie for good, and this breaks Frankies heart as he had taught the young boxer everything he knows.

The story thickens, there is much more to it than boxing. Million Dollar Baby is full of emotional power and great Acting from the three main characters. The three main charcaters are Frankie who runs a boxing gym, Morgan Freeman who is called Scrap which is also an old man, that was actually trained by Frankie way back until in one fight Scrap lost his eye. Scrap has been living at the gym over the Years now, and he pritty much is the guy that is always there to help Frankie through the hard times, talks Frankie into doing things and he also helps clean up around the gym.

The third Main ""Actress"" is played by Hilary Swank and she plays as Maggie, Maggie is the main event in this movie. One day at the gym Scrap tells Frankie that there is a young lady in his gym hitting a boxing bag. Frankie than goes down and asks her what she is doing here, and than Maggie just straight up says that she wants to be the Best Boxer in the World, and than she casually asks Frankie if he would train her. Frankie says No he dosent train girls and that there are other trainers that would take her on, Maggie than disagrees and says that he is the only guy that could get her to the top, and thats because she has seen him training previous boxers and she knows that he is 100% dedicated to his job. Im not going to spoil anything that happens, so dont think that im going to so I will just simplify on some details. Frankie dosent want to train this Girl, tho Scrap convinces him otherwise and now from this point on in the film Frankie teaches everything he knows to Maggie and they both start to have a real emotional bond.

Maggie and Frankie become very close friends, to the point where Frankie would never want to see her get hurt, and plus Frankie always reminds her throughtout the film that she needs to always defend her self and never put her guard down. Unfortunately when Maggie does finally make her way to the championship, something terrible happens at the fight. Maggie lets down her guard, and im not going to give anything away,tho there is something that happens that changes her life and Frankies life forever.

From this point on in the Film it becomes very emotional and Powerful. I was just watching a very interesting and very meaningful film about a Under-dog Boxer which eventually rises to the top with a trainer always by her side to help her get there. Now the film has all been brought to an entire new level, I am feeling sad at what im watching tho I think its wonderful at what happens at the end. I think that anybody so close to someone and that has always been there for them would want to do the same thing that Frankie does at the end. Million Dollar baby is honestely one of my Favouite Movies of all time, it has so much power throughout it, and I can tell that the actors and Clint Eastwood all used there hearts when making this film, and thats because there is nothing wrong with this film at all. Everything in Million Dollar Baby is excellent including all the fight scenes, the dramatic scenes, and the Amazing ending. This also is the best and most realistic Acting ive seen from Clint Eastwood, You can honestely feel the happiness he goes through, The sadness and the loss he goes through as its all there for us viewers to witness. I recommend this to everyone that hasnt seen it and for the People that already have. This is a Masterpiece with a capital M.

RATING- MASTERPIECE","1caa4998-cf68-447d-9950-0584f9fcbae5",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-11-22","","RT","901673490"
