4.5,"Definitely one of Clint Eastwood's finest performances as an actor and as a director. Sure, it seems Eastwood plays the same curmudgeon hardass in every film he was in the last 25 years but this time as Frankie Dunn, it really fit. While I love Morgan Freeman, his role as Scrap does not even go into his top ten best performances. Freeman was much better in Driving Miss Daisy, The Shawshank Redemption, Glory, and Lean On Me to name a few. However, Hilary Swank was excellent as the tough Maggie Fitzgerald and she definitely deserved her second Academy Award win. Swank is one of the most underrated actresses right now and all her talents came to life in this film. One of the 20 best films I have seen in the last 10 years.","5d9b0c9e-77ab-4e4a-aef1-58bf1b06a75f",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-12-30","","RT","783648637"
3.0,"To be honest, Million Dollar Baby was a slight disappointment. Though performances were admirable (Morgan Freeman was probably the most worthy of praise) and the storyline was clever, it felt a little too conventional for my taste. My biggest quibble is that from Maggie's accident onwards, the film seemed to take a detour, and felt very disjointed from the first half, and a tad overblown. In contrast, the interesting backstory of Frankie's relationship with his daughter seemed a bit of an afterthought, and could have done with more development. In many aspects, some scenes just missed the mark. Though promising and with some good moments, it required more character development from the script and was too straightforward.","6a8092a0-2e7e-431a-b725-b22d87a70b16",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2011-01-01","","RT","905480611"
