4.5,"Clint Eastwood has become a master at delivering dark & moody drama's, this film adds so much depth and complexity to each character and the story is steeped in the harsh realities of life. So much so that this film transcends the genre of the typical inspirational boxing movie. Frankie Dunn (Clint Eastwood) is a seasoned boxing trainer and owner of a gym who has more than a few demons in his past. One day he crosses paths with a stubborn and determined woman who's only goal in life is to become a boxer and relentlessly pursues Dunn to train her. But the equally stubborn Frankie Dunn turns her down because he refuses to train women and is convinced that she has just missed her window of opportunity because of her age. But when she won't give up and keeps coming to his gym, she eventually wears him down and he agrees to train her. The storyline and the acting in this film are just flawless, but again this isn't your typical inspiration type movie as it takes you to some very dark places in it's exploration of each character's own humanity.","55505600-1462-4f02-98d8-31886e1dfa12",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2011-05-30","","RT","905819848"
3.0,"Good not great...deeply depressing story, wonderfully acted.","992761a5-698d-4ca3-b367-8f45e6e6db81",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2011-05-30","","RT","861988579"
5.0,"Clint Eastwood is capable of making a perfect film, and this one is just that. With an all-star cast, brilliant acting, and one hell of a memorable yet sad story, this film is a masterpiece. Clint just has this way of storytelling that pulls you in right from the start and does not let go until the very end. Narration from Morgan Freeman made it that much better. A must see. A+","7a57ea58-ceeb-41f0-b7f4-159f788f594c",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-06-06","","RT","895963934"
