2.5,"I remember all of the Oscar buzz this got back in it's time. I'm pretty sure that was mainly due to the star combination of Clint Eastwood, Hilary Swank and Morgan Freeman. All of them are powerful performers for sure, and they enforced that fact in this film. However I'm just not a die-hard fan of sports flicks. They almost always follow the underdog plot arc. Sure this one put a twist on it by making the underdog a female boxer, but she was still an unlikely candidate from a very poor background. It was kind of nice how Frankie and Maggie sort of formed this father-daughter relationship in absence of real, caring family of their own. The whole bit about euthanasia at the end did put a new emotional dimension on the story as well. However this movie was just too conventional to win my love. I think most of the respect given to this film is just out of homage to Clint Eastwood's work at such an old age.","0913593c-867b-4f68-a14c-b84bed448c94",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2011-09-24","","RT","781957090"
