3.0,"While this is a good movie, something about it is a bit off. I just cannot pinpoint what exactly that something is. It isn't the actors, they're great - well, what did you expect from Clint Eastwood and Morgan Freeman - in Hilary Swank's case, surprisingly so. Some of the plot twists are a bit rough around the edges, but the story itself isn't that bad - though at some points it feels a bit rushed. The undertones are okay, the side characters are pretty standard - meaning not bad - and the settings are okay as well. So really, what is there not to like? Well, I don't know, but for some reason I really didn't enjoy this as much as I could have had that something not been there bothering me. Perhaps it's just that the movie tries to be so realistically and cleanly told that it loses something along the way. Actually, the word clinical is perfect to describe this film. It's a good film and you should watch it, but it's still a bit clinical.","688e4a01-bb21-40ed-8aad-5f30e52f3821",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2011-10-11","","RT","915749595"
3.0,"There's no denying Eastwood can do it all, but I feel that in this instance many viewers allowed their great love and respect for the cinematic veteran to blind their judgement of this flawed movie. Million Dollar Baby has its moments but ultimately this is a maudlin, corny and often dull affair. Its emotions may run deep, but the poorly paced screenplay and sports-movie sentimentalism rarely create the spark needed to allow such emotion to properly impact on the viewer. The performances are good, but again don't seem to have the impact on me that they did for others. This is a competent and well-made film from the great director, but certainly not the Oscar-worthy masterpiece that many regard it to be.","df4712c3-a4ed-419b-ae8d-4f18d0b108ef",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2011-10-11","","RT","905967776"
5.0,"Million Dollar Baby My nutshell Review

This is one of the greatest films of all time. A very shaking story of a wanna be boxer which ends her up in complete failure and death. Clinton Eastwood gives his best shot as the trainer who hopelessly can't get anyone to their title shot but when he gets a boxer that too a woman he does a big small mistake which takes toll of her whole life and career. Hilary swank plays one of her best as Maggie Fitzgerald the woman who wanted to be a boxer even at a late age of 32 as she believed life hadn't given her anything and as this was her chance to get something out of it. The Montage is excellent and you will be visually stunned by the degree of perfection of the direction by Clint Eastwood. This movie is really powerful and leaves you an inspirational message at the courage of Maggie to get out of this world the hard way. The script of the movie is great and some dialogues really convey something more than what they mean. Morgan Freeman plays one of his best as a boxer who had become a one eyed man because of a mistake which Frankie had committed. What can happen inside a family of dirty money loving morons were explicitly shown and those scenes were emotionally wrenching. It's a very straight forward approach which anyone can love and this is one of the best films of the Decade.

My rating : A+","bb4048f3-a3e2-4974-b5e1-b132ad45ea80",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-10-11","","RT","910485546"
