3.0,"Eastwood's style may be subtle, but this script is anything but. Everyone is pretty much a caricature, especially the supporting characters of Maggie's mother, Danger, the priest, and whoever Anthony Mackie was supposed to be. The movie intentionally kills its upward momentum with about 40 minutes to go in order to keep the dirge-like feeling of this heavy film. Obviously Swank and Freeman are good, and Clint is, well, Clint. The movie is pretty enough to look at though it can be a tad dull at times - the same can be said of the story. There's nothing really awful here but not much to get excited about either. Decent drama.","e4d036b8-f85c-4d5d-b452-eafd96e184c4",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2011-12-01","","RT","786798969"
