4.5,"Definitely one of Clint Eastwood's finest performances as an actor and as a director. Sure, it seems Eastwood plays the same curmudgeon hardass in every film he was in the last 25 years but this time as Frankie Dunn, it really fit. While I love Morgan Freeman, his role as Scrap does not even go into his top ten best performances. Freeman was much better in Driving Miss Daisy, The Shawshank Redemption, Glory, and Lean On Me to name a few. However, Hilary Swank was excellent as the tough Maggie Fitzgerald and she definitely deserved her second Academy Award win. Swank is one of the most underrated actresses right now and all her talents came to life in this film. One of the 20 best films I have seen in the last 10 years.","a9a992c0-6ed4-44dc-9087-b620d133fb33",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2012-02-12","","RT","836409280"
4.0,"This is not one of those strive-till-you-thrive sports flicks in which being happy and successful is all that matters. It's about listening to your own heart and your instincts fearlessly enough for the world to know that how lead your life is none of their business, it's about letting them know that come hell or high water, you'll stick to you guns.. The movie also sheds a light on the nastily inconsiderate side of human nature and its oft-concealed crude primitiveness. Acting-wise, Hilary Swank shines like a star, and both Freeman and even Eastwood are flawlessly good.","5f8fe1ba-af24-4261-9521-f9738f93b3ea",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2012-02-13","","RT","906584824"
