4.5,"The first part of this movie left me wondering why this picture won a Best Picture. It was a feel-good boxing flick, nothing more. Sure, it had that powerful voice-over from Morgan Freeman, that could add gravity to anything and make the Yellow Pages sound interesting, and Swank and Eastwood performed well, but there was nothing special there.

And then, the closing act. The final round. That's where the emotion comes in, where all the parts come together in one insanely depressing, tragic conclusion. I won't give too many details, in case any readers of this are yet to see the film, but definitely see it, and don't give up on it early.

Eastwood is fast becoming one of my favourite directors.","1c1099a1-0a02-4f76-a78b-9658f3af1592",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2012-03-07","","RT","913510543"
