5.0,"I gave this a blu-ray purchase last week, and after watching again last night I realize this is one of my favorite movies of all time. Swank, Eastwood, and Freeman all deliver powerful performances while taking you on an emotional ride through a boxer's journey to the top and beyond. I prefer this to Gran Torino, Changeling, and Mystic River: all excellent films directed by Eastwood that I consider some of the best of the past decade. If you missed this, add it to your queue sometime soon.","bbb0a235-d444-49a7-9d1c-a04f4d40bda7",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2012-03-17","","RT","922157444"
5.0,"Surpassing the derivative nature of the genre, Million Dollar Baby is profoundly sincere and heart-breaking with confident direction from Clint Eastwood together with sensational performances from Hilary Swank and Morgan Freeman.","c2dbb1ef-f58d-4717-add0-5e2cba72f542",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2012-03-17","","RT","906546627"
4.5,"This is Clint Eastwood's masterpiece! Everything fell into place to make this one of the most stunning films I have ever seen in my life. This film has incredible acting, great directing, and one of the most inspirational and heartbreaking stories. It deserves all the claim and rewards it has received. This could have been another simplistic story about a boxer trying to make it big. Instead, it delves deep into the emotion of the characters and their lives. One of the few films that almost made me cry. The only thing that does not make it completely perfect is the ending feels somewhat drawn out. However, the ending leaves you close to tears with the level of emotion the actors portray in their roles. To any Clint Eastwood fan, this is one of the movies you need to see immediately.","0cae9395-d866-4e23-b60c-08e92a7c14e9",False,True,False,False,4.5,"2012-03-18","","RT","904384757"
4.5,"Clint Eastwood has become a master at delivering dark & moody drama's, this film adds so much depth and complexity to each character and the story is steeped in the harsh realities of life. So much so that this film transcends the genre of the typical inspirational boxing movie. Frankie Dunn (Clint Eastwood) is a seasoned boxing trainer and owner of a gym who has more than a few demons in his past. One day he crosses paths with a stubborn and determined woman who's only goal in life is to become a boxer and relentlessly pursues Dunn to train her. But the equally stubborn Frankie Dunn turns her down because he refuses to train women and is convinced that she has just missed her window of opportunity because of her age. But when she won't give up and keeps coming to his gym, she eventually wears him down and he agrees to train her. The storyline and the acting in this film are just flawless, but again this isn't your typical inspiration type movie as it takes you to some very dark places in it's exploration of each character's own humanity.","31635bab-6804-4f60-bde4-f7b6645782a9",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2012-03-21","","RT","843361122"
4.5,"A truely masterful film. Incredible performances from Eastwood, Swank, and Freeman, as well as the rest of the cast. Million Dollar Baby is a touching, sad, and very well made and genuine film, a true example of Clint Eastwood's genius (as actor and director). This is a must-see film.","cf9621e1-200c-4c1d-be10-c92dda046272",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2012-03-21","","RT","911471637"
