3.5,"Million Dollar Baby begins like a typical sports movie (I thought it was going to be the female Rocky, which got me thinking - didn't Hilary already do this with The Karate Kid?), but ends up being a very engrossing tale about the family-like relationship between fighter and coach. The best scenes involve Swank and Freeman, ever the impeccable actors who know how to carry a moment through. Eastwood, while a wonderful director, didn't compel me as much, but did a good enough job. The overall arc of the film works beautifully, depicting some of the trials and triumphs of life. Other moments, however, suffer from American cinematicism, with overly simplified characters (Swank's mother, for example) that seem to pull away from the morer sincere core of the film. Still, it is an endearing and gripping story worth watching.","ad200d30-3b17-472f-8249-0de095a6aa8b",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2012-09-22","","RT","791217159"
