5.0,"If someone tells you the story about a woman struggling to pay rent who wishes to become a boxer, you probably wont be interested. Only someone like Clint Eastwood can create from such a simple story one of the most amazing movies ever made making you feel that you want to be a part of it. Even the small roles of the movie like Danger (Jay Baruchel) were done perfectly as if competing for an Oscar, the small conversations between Eastwood and Freeman like when they were talking about the cheap bleach might seem unimportant but this shows you how even smallest details didn't slip away  from the movie to make you feel there struggle. Usually movies with happy endings sell easier but this time Clint Eastwood proved this wrong by having the guts to end the movie in the most dramatic way possible. To sum this up, its a blessing we have such a movie in these times where childish and unprofessional movies usually take the lead. All I can say if you want to be a director, than watch and learn because this is a movie that  can be watched in every era.","d996799c-a292-427d-aae5-d1c672db1247",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2013-07-01","","RT","943122784"
