4.5,"A quality, well-made boxing drama which produces such a mix of emotional punches that you'll immediately become immersed in it's story. I like the style in which Clint Eastwood performs his tough exterior but soft interior character. It worked well in 'Gran Torino' and it works well here. Morgan Freeman relives 'Shawshank Redemption' and offers his distinct soothing voice for narration as well as serving as a great supporting actor in his role as an partly blind retired boxer. This reflects his better days before he made the switch to assassin/old smug pimp roles (i.e. 'Wanted' and 'Now you see Me'). Hilary Swank could not have done much better as the confident main protagonist; definitely worthy of her Academy Award and Golden Globe. Most notably however is the powerful ending. It is bound to pull your heart strings whilst delivering the final knockout blow to send 'Million Dollar Baby' into award-winning territory. Bravo.","785e70db-440b-431d-867a-5233dad450e1",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-12-22","","RT","828383746"
