3.5,"Million Dollar Baby is a very sad and very harrowing movie about a female boxer. I remember seeing this movie when I was 12 with my parents and I don't think I liked it then because I was too young to understand it. My parents covered my eyes through most of it because of the violent fighting scenes. Million Dollar Baby is about a struggling woman, Maggie Fitzgerald (Hilary Swank) who has one big passion, to be a female boxer. She asks Frankie Dunn (Clint Eastwood), a boxing trainer to train her. At first he refuses and won't take her seriously because she is a woman and he doesn't believe that boxing is a sport suitable for women. Eventually he reluctantly decides to train her. Maggie is also helped along the way by retired boxer Eddie ""Scrap Iron"" Dupris (Morgan Freeman), who also narrates the story. Maggie becomes extremely successful and her career climbs great heights, but is her career in boxing ill-fated?

The leads were powerful and strong; Hilary Swank, Clint Eastwood and Morgan Freeman were phenomenal. Clint Eastwood is a very talented man, not only did he act in the film, he also directed it. This film is also quite unique in that female boxing isn't really that popular and boxing films are usually about men in the ring, not women. This film is quite dark and harrowing and has a lot of violent and blood, so if you don't like dark and depressing films with lots of violence this probably isn't for you. I have to admit myself that I found that film a bit too dark, but it was very moving with outstanding performances from the cast. I like how the film tells us about Maggie's life and background; her primitive hillbilly family are un-supportive and only want Maggie's money. This is a really powerful drama, though don't see it if you're feeling low.

Grade: A-/B+","b66757a0-dc66-4490-b9ce-9827fd08ebd6",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2014-01-24","","RT","938161461"
4.0,"As a fan of the sweet science, it is a little odd that I put off seeing this film for as long as I did. Hilary Swank is an aging waitress but wants more out of her life, so she starts going to a boxing gym in hopes she'll be trained. After much pestering, Clint Eastwood finally agrees to train her. Having problems with his own daughter, he sort of develops a new father/daughter relationship with her. He helps her from her small fights all the way up to her bigger fights until she gets sucker punched and gets injured. Her life quickly deteriorates since she is entirely bed-ridden and has to live a machine assisted life. I can agree with some of the criticisms that she wins in such an odd way of always knocking her opponents out. Also, her final opponent would have been disqualified long before the sucker punch for her actions. Besides those things, I enjoyed this. It was a touching story and one of the better Eastwood directed movies which are mostly very good.","6685ad67-d0f5-4386-8fde-f3e116f47dbc",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2014-01-27","","RT","781879239"
3.5,"""SWANK WILL KNOCK YOU OUT""  

- Four Academy Award winning 'Million Dollar Baby' is a 2004 sports drama by and with living legend Clint Eastwood (Dirty Harry films). He brings a strong and emotional story about a young woman trying to make her dream of becoming a boxer come true. Normally not my cup of tea, but I found it to be extremely powerful. This film ran more than half a year in the American movie theaters. Next to Eastwood, we see Morgan Freeman (Seven). But I have a huge respect for the amazing performance of Hillary Swank (Boys Don't Cry). A must see piece of art. 

 After losing his prize winning protégé to a successful manager, grumpy old boxing trainer Frankie Dunn (Eastwood) is approached by waitress Maggie Fitzgerald (Swank) to train her. Telling her he doesn't train girls, she doesn't stop coming over to the gym that Frankie runs with the help from 'Scrap' (Freeman), who encourages her. Eventually Frankie agrees to teach her some tricks. Maggie turns out to be a very talented and hard training woman. Being estranged from his own daughter, Frankie develops a bond with her and arranges her first boxing fight. It doesn't take long before she becomes a professional and they travel to Europe where she keeps on winning. With the prize money she wants to buy her white trash family (who are living in a trailer park) a real house. But during the most important match, that is settled for one million dollar, tragedy strikes and the lives of Frankie and Maggie will never be the same...","d39fb57e-841f-415a-8306-2783f6ae200d",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2014-02-04","","RT","932330288"
3.0,"A film with higher ambitions than results, not unlike Swank's character. Million Dollar Baby offers really great performances from its cast and delivers a fantastic start, but then gradually fades away halfway through and becomes a bit too melodramatic and boring for my taste. There is strong production design and cinematography. I want to love this film, but rewatching it now 10 years after it's debut, it shows it's flaws more now that the. Oscar shine has dulled a bit.","551cdd20-9032-4953-8611-9e606036841a",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2014-02-08","","RT","873935102"
5.0,"A near perfect movie. I was reluctant to watch it because I am not a big Hillary Swank fan. But this movie is just incredible. I cant find anything negative to say about it.","bf617c94-4c5c-457d-91c7-96840b18d86e",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-02-16","","RT","911599366"
3.0,"It works on more levels than it fails in the end, mostly, in the second two thirds. The first third was incoherent. I couldn't really get into what was going on... It felt like at that point the movie wasn't sure what it wanted to be, so it tried a few things. Scenes feel out of place, and characters do things out of character. It just confused me. And it felt a bit obnoxious, cliched, and stale on the editing side. For the most part, the next two thirds worked really well, a few minor flaws aside, but it doesn't completely make up for the first half. We get a really powerful performance here though, well done Hilary Swank.","18167fc2-f6ff-4e30-a6bf-75dfd56e586c",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2014-02-17","","RT","925917533"
