5.0,"Gaspingly moving and downright heart-wrenching, this sports drama earned the veteran cast 3 Oscar nods, winning two along with a best picture nod. Every minute of this film, fast and slow, shows the true compassion for the love of the sport along with the everlasting ties of the friendship between a teacher and student. Eastwood again directs a magnificent heartfelt movie that is both family friendly and can attract all ages of all kinds. The plot focuses on how sacrifices are made in order to find the true value in life. True colors are spilled from each character when nothing else can be sacrificed by the end of the film. Million Dollar Baby will make you feel paralyzed from the neck down as your eyes cannot leave the film due to the spectacular screenplay and heart put into this unforgettable adventure. 5 stars.","72ef2a74-402e-4086-9310-abf5dfbca3b6",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-08-11","","RT","966262821"
4.0,"Before ""Gran Torino"" came out, I thought this was Clint Eastwood's best movie. This is a very heartfelt movie, with a very beautiful story attached to it. Clint Eastwood in my opinion gives the best performance of his career in the movie. He gives a very stern, but emotional performance in the film especially towards the end of the movie where you just see his performance pour out of him. I've never seen Eastwood cry before in a movie, so when I saw this movie and towards the end of the movie where he opens up to the priest in the film about Hilary Swank, I had never been so shocked by a performance by him before and he usually plays the tough guy roles that he is know for like ""Dirty Harry"" and ""Gran Torino."" But in this movie he gives a very human performance in the movie, definitely making him worthy of the best actor nomination that year for the movie. But it's his keen eye directing that makes his performance and the movie work so well. Hilary Swank also steps up to the plate with Eastwood and also gives in my opinion the best performance of her career in the movie. I knew as soon as I saw the movie she was gonna win best actress that year at the oscars. She so good you can't take your eyes off her as you root for the entire movie. And also for Morgan Freeman, who has screen legend written all over him, gives an awesome supporting performance in the film as Eastwood's longest and closest boxing friend in the film, who he trained and managed him in a fight years ago when Freeman and Eastwood were young men and Freeman was I. His prime as a boxer before losing his eye in a boxing match for getting hit too hard. The whole film is compelling to watch until it gets to the end with Swank's character as the movie becomes very emotional to sit through and watch. It's the final act that earned the movie it's Best Picture win and Best Director for Clint Eastwood who deserved the award without a doubt that year. I definitely rank this as one of the best boxing movies of all time even though it's from a woman's perspective but who cares, the movie is pure magic all the way through the end; and I don't say that about a lot of movies.","eff8f04c-2024-424c-89c4-67011b59129a",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2014-08-21","","RT","969946135"
4.5,"It will repel misogynists and those who are dissatisfied with films that are not 100% sugary but Million Dollar Baby proves an enriching and emotional powerhouse of a movie with grand, dramatic narrative and dedicated acting from its three absorbing leads.","2943f465-1048-4c73-a890-35162f66c79d",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2014-08-25","","RT","905522919"
5.0,"There aren't many word to describe this film, few come to mind such as a masterpiece which clearly fits the film. What I thought would be a typical sports movie turns out to be the best sports movie I have seen. Moneyball used to be my favorite sports film but this takes the spot due to great acting and an astounding story with a great twist. The character development for the 3 main characters was amazing, through out the movie I cared for them and got interested in them. This film has 4 oscars and I think they are well deserved. The only flaw I saw was that the fight scenes were getting repetitive and predictable but that's a microscopic minor flaw. The film does a great job of blending comedy with drama. Overall form it's knockouts to its story this is a must see film.","904bb9e7-ce1a-4eab-ae6a-51f9dd84e0df",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-09-16","","RT","926701522"
5.0,"This movie was a masterpiece. Eastwood pulled a jack-of-all-trades to make  film that is more inspirational and emotional than any Rocky film. Him, Swank, and Freeman were nothing short of phenomenal and the devastating third act is an unstoppable force. This is one of the greatest movies of all time.","3ce274ef-1e5c-4648-a040-bc225d7312bc",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-10-04","","RT","916389780"
5.0,"If you enjoy movies about love, strength, and sadness, the 2004 movie Million Dollar Baby is a movie you should see. It has a 91% rating on Rotten Tomatoes, a score of 86 on Metacritic, and it reached an 8.1/10 on IMDb. It was won numerous awards including Best Picture at the 77th Academy Awards. Clint Eastwood also won his second Best Director Oscar for this film, which was very much deserved, considering he directed, co-produced, and also played a major role in the movie as well.
	Million Dollar Baby is a sports drama. It is about a girl named Maggie, played by Hilary Swank. She is a waitress in a small and run-down city in Missouri. Maggie aspires to be a boxer but when she shows up at an old gym in Los Angeles, she is let down when she asks the owner to train her. The gym owner, Frankie, played by Clint Eastwood, doesn't take long to answer her question; ""I don't train girls"". Even though she is the only woman in the gym, she continues to show up every day and train herself until someone helps her. After seeing her persistence and the way that she was embarrassing herself due to the little knowledge she had, Frankie agreed to teach her the basics of boxing until he could find her a manager. He finds her a manager and she is set for her first fight. During the fight, Maggie is not doing so well and Frankie takes the new manager's place and coaches her through the fight instead. After being persuaded by his friend Scrap, played by Morgan Freeman, and after spending time watching Maggie in the ring, Frankie realizes she is a natural and that he wants to work with her. Frankie had a rough past with his own daughter, and he feels he could build a father-daughter bond with Maggie. Maggie's own family isn't very caring and doesn't show her much support so she gladly builds a relationship with Frankie. Frankie sets up a very important fight for Maggie, even though he is very protective of her at this point and has been reluctant to let her fight. The fight is in Las Vegas against the WBA champion. Maggie is doing well in the fight when all of a sudden she gets knocked out and falls on the stool in the corner of the ring, breaking her neck. This leaves a very bad outlook for the rest of her career. When she tries to call her family, no one ever answers. Finally one day they show up to the hospital to see her on their way back from Disneyland. They also have a lawyer with them to try and get Maggie to sign all of her money over to them. Maggie orders them to leave. It is at this moment when she realizes how much Frankie cares about her. 
	The movie has a dark setting. The gym, the place Maggie works, and the hospital are all dark and gloomy. This is to enhance that it is in a run-down part of town, and it is not meant to be a cheerful movie. The volume of the movie is very dim compared to other movies. When Frankie talks, you have to turn the volume up just to understand him. This gives more of a dark and sad effect also. Throughout the movie, Morgan Freeman is also narrating. Any movie that involves Morgan Freeman is automatically a must-see. Morgan Freeman was perfect for this role because his smooth and slow voice helps to set the gloomy tone for the movie. 
	The main theme of this movie is if you try hard enough and if you don't give up on something, even though others are criticizing and laughing at you, you can achieve anything you set your mind to. Maggie came from a small and poor city and her family didn't believe in her because of their own confidence issues, and she still managed to get herself out there and was persistent and diligent when it came to getting what she wanted. Frankie went through his whole life being depressed and guilty about his daughter that he never got to know, and this made him not want to train girls or build any relationship with a young girl. But once he took the chance, it was the best thing for him and Maggie cheered him up constantly and she made him very proud of her accomplishments, just as a father would be.","47453605-c3b1-4538-bd29-8498ff1bf015",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-10-06","","RT","966984486"
5.0,"98% Really the best Movie you will see from Clint Eastwood, Million Dollar Baby is what really will be his true legacy as a Director. This Movie will arguably will be the best from the Legend Morgan Freeman, as being his only Oscar. Hilary Swank delivers again, in her second Oscar winning role, this is truly the Movie of the Year, and one of the Movies of the Decade.","199bbbab-50d0-41de-8454-be51c382d216",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-10-25","","RT","923878256"
5.0,"A superbly acted Sports Drama and outstandingly directed by the legendary Clint Eastwood. Million Dollar Baby defines itself as a touching unforgettable  movie with memorable characters. 

Eastwood stars as the legendary boxing trainer Frankie Dunn, who in is elderly years, is a gym owner. When a young lady, called Maggie Fitzgerald, enters his life and his gym to gain the experience and technique required to make it to the title and become a major boxing champion, she's turned down by Frankie whose got little faith in female boxers. Quitting is not an option for Maggie when she believes it's her only chance to see a bright future ahead of her. Frankie eventually decides to train her. This movie also stars Morgan Freeman in a great supporting role as Frankie's best friend Eddie Dupris, a former fighter who Frankie trained.

It's, undoubtedly, an forgettable masterpiece and a great achievement in directing for Eastwood. The Oscar nominations and wins for this movie are well deserved and Morgan Freeman's narration in this movie is excellent and heartfelt - just the way it was in The Shawshank Redemption. The Oscar he won for Best Supporting Actor in this movie is well deserved and it's one of the best movies of his career. When I watched this I never heard of Hilary Swank before, but she played Maggie in a way that I could relate to because if I knew someone like her I'd pity her and look up to her, so Hilary definitely earned that Oscar she won. The last two out of the four Oscars it won was for Best Picture and Director - both for Eastwood. A genius whose brought a genius movie to life!","54ba4090-195e-49b8-b1c4-10340c635f62",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-10-27","","RT","927860359"
2.0,"Yeah, great performances from the cast, but if you think about it, what message does this movie send to everyone? If you've been paralyzed from an injury, then there's no point to go on living? Just end it? NO! 
