3.5,"A well acted film about a female wanting to fulfill who dream of boxing. Believing its the only thing she ever felt good doing. We see Hilary Swank and Clint Eastwood relationship develop throughout. Its like a Dad and daughter relationship that they both lack. Swank's life show how her family live in poverty and on the state and all she has is boxing. Eastwood is the old coach who we that Swank is his life chance. Freeman narrates and his relationship with Eastwood is very believable as they both have lived through boxing all their lives and they still have little funny digs at each other. The boxing are fine, they are not the best boxing scenes ever filmed and watching Swank's character many fights in one round at times becomes boring. The last twenty minutes is where a lot of the emotion kicks in. Without boxing what is Swank's life, and what will Eastwood's character becomes the moral dilemma. Its quite a depressing end to the film, and i am not quite sure what it wanted to say. I didn't want or expect a Rocky ending. I am glad it didn't go an easy way but i don't think it fully worked. Winning the Oscars i am not totally convinced, i believe Eastwood, Swank and Freeman have done better movies. Freeman narrates just feeling like many other movies. A good movie but not one that i will want to watch again soon.","25996ed5-2d85-4188-8e48-8a4a71fb5513",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2020-06-20","","RT","978664196"
