4.0,"We return to Clint Eastwood's universe with Million Dollar Baby, a sports film which could be a gender-swapped version of Rocky, but really it's anything but. Maggie Fitzgerald (Hilary Swank) wants to become one of the great welterweight contenders and recruits trainer Frankie (Clint Eastwood), who at first refuses but eventually has a change of heart, and his best friend Scrap-Iron Dupris (Morgan Freeman). Similarly like Rocky, this is another one of those movies where the winner loses in the end, except Million's resolution is less balanced because Maggie gets paralyzed, has her leg amputated and begs for mercy killing. Also, this movie could easily have been sugar-coated with gender politics, with all the men in the gym being powerless over the female boxer. Instead, Eastwood takes a more liberal and realistic approach, focusing on Frankie's quest for redemption. While, yes, Maggie gets taken for granted and harassed by fellow gym members, her Ozark heart is part-iron, as she bites back with her slam comebacks. However, it's the ending that serves as the movie's saving grace. Frankie unplugs Maggie's respiratory machine and disappears into the diner, unable to return to his old profession anymore. Meanwhile, Scrap-Iron reminisces about Frankie's departure, holds his friend's torch at the gym and reads his daughter's letters. So, Million Dollar Baby isn't just a generic sports drama, it's a study of success and retirement. 

(4 Sleeping Socks with Holes on Them out of 5)","0c60f06a-6e9e-4c0b-9ff1-240e05fe9cd6",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2020-07-23","","RT","909109136"
5.0,"never cried at a movie so hard, i think the way the director isolated Hilary and clints relationship made the movie sad at the end. I'm so glad they didn't give Hillary character some cheesy cliche abusive boyfriend or gave clint a mean wife or something. 100/10 everyone should watch this","49417ea6-899c-4cbf-9b9a-3d300538abd1",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2020-08-08","","RT","978644669"
