5.0,"Apart from the ‘nineties' expected Morgan Freeman narrative (does make you think you're watching Shawshank, but only for about twelve seconds) this is just the most beautiful film I have ever seen. The connection between Eastwood and Swank is, literally, beyond words...I thought it was about boxing,.,,I have never witnessed such a moving love story on screen...And being a daughter of a fine man, I am so happy to say that Eastwood's character couldn't have shown more of the love of a Dad. He really really loves her. 

I want to find that fucking bitch who punched Maggie after the bell. I will claw that evil whores eyes out with my own acrylic nails...Even though this film is ten years old.  I actually hope she never worked as an actress again EVER..Which is utterly ridiculous because we are, after all, speaking about movies... 

If this film was a kind of large egg, I would swallow it whole, and poach it in my soul....and then I would actually put a pen in my eye just to make sure that the bitch of a mother is dead....(Clearly another amazing actress)

One hundred million  kajillion for this one. I'm so in love with Frankie and Maggie. Dramatically in love xxx","66e8391d-a9ba-4338-adc2-ea73aad00ea5",False,False,False,True,5.0,"2020-08-14","","RT","978808859"
5.0,"An emotionally powered drama, combined with Eastwood's direction, Hallis and Toole's script, the performances of the cast, Eastwood's score, Stern's cinematography, Cox's editing, Bumstead's production design, Goddard's set decoration, Hopper's costume design, emotional weight and themes, Million Dollar Baby ranks highly amongst the films to win the Oscar for Best Picture!!!","5684ea35-1682-480a-9dd9-06039795049f",False,False,False,True,5.0,"2020-08-19","Cody M","RT","87cc253b-bc96-44e9-93ec-9684a03a2198"
