4.0,"Hilary Swank does a brilliant performance as boxing late bloomer Maggie, and in my opinion both old male actors aren't far behind. It's all basically well balanced, in a way that it's easy to tell that everyone in the production team have had a good time. However, it actually feels like a mistake to call it a sports drama, as Million Dollar Baby is about so much more other than boxing. This is no Rocky. The main characters are so superb, so having some pathetic and rather silly side characters being over due in their mission to create a contrast to the story feels sometimes unnecessary. Nevertheless, Eastwood knows how to press the emotional buttons, particularly in the final, and anyone who has seen One Flew Over the Cockoo's Nest or Betty Blue 37*C, knows where he found the inspiration.","9ba483d0-4472-4c9b-83d5-2b2e272790c3",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2021-12-15","","RT","3e0e6aaa-b50d-4073-8ffa-5ae8bbb5a54d"
0.5,"Not even Hillary Swank's great acting can save this terrible movie. Just under the surface lurk a barrage of reactionary themes (not surprising, considering who the director is), paired with an apparent disdain for the lower class. Also, aren't we all sick of the same old trite ""disposable woman"" trope? ""The male protagonist grows and learns valuable lessons through the death/terrible tragedy of the female character"". Just give me a break.","c15a167f-63dc-4c75-8208-9171a1e51bf5",False,False,False,False,0.5,"2022-01-15","Rita D","RT","777242c0-61a3-4624-8deb-5df85408d01d"
5.0,"Where do I even begin? Hillary Swank, Clint Eastwood, and Morgan Freeman. Are you kidding me? This movie is amazing from start to finish. The plot is amazing and the accompanying script is gold. It is one of those movies where you want to show it to everyone who hasn't seen it. Hillary Swank deserves the World for this role. She captured the essence of Maggie Fitzgerald in ways words can not describe. Let's not forget about a strong performance, albeit short, from Margot Martindale. Beautiful, beautiful movie.","bacac728-1a62-4e0d-a7fc-bcc6847e8993",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2022-01-20","","RT","979448980"
5.0,"Unreal! I didn't expect 'Million Dollar Baby' to be so astonishingly brilliant.

I've said it many a time before but for full context, I do not read up about films before watching them - aside from making sure the film isn't part of a franchise, checking the run time and seeing the genre - so I was expecting this to be a cliché-filled, but still great, sports flick. It's so much more than that.

It's way more deeper and has an everlasting impact that I hadn't anticipated. Even across the opening chunk I was predicating the obvious cliché ending, but as the film progresses and, especially, as the final portion rolls around it just absorbed my total attention - I was fully engrossed... hook, line, and sinker. Some film!

The cast are simply stunning. Clint Eastwood gives an absolutely fantastic performance, Hilary Swank is truly sensational - especially at the end, damn - and Morgan Freeman is Morgan Freeman; what an actor and what a voice, using him as narrator was a great move. Elsewhere, and though less dramatically, Jay Baruchel, Anthony Mackie, Margo Martindale and Michael Peña also feature interestingly.

It's quite the journey the film takes you on, which I just found utterly enthralling to watch unfold. Perfect pacing, perfect acting. I loved watching every second of it and will undoubtedly be revisiting it.

I noted days ago that I was rather surprised to learn that Eastwood's 'Unforgiven' had been so heavily acclaimed, on this occasion with this 2004 film I am the complete opposite. I don't care much for awards et al., but I am delighted to see all involved receive their props for this. Chapeau!

Marvellous, just marvellous.","aa6487b3-8b01-4c2d-9834-5367c6e5b630",False,False,False,True,5.0,"2022-02-09","r 9","RT","80d5b0ca-1f0e-47cb-8ae2-06bfbb141d2e"
