4.5,"Frankie, an ill-tempered old coach, reluctantly agrees to train aspiring boxer Maggie. Impressed with her determination and talent, he helps her become the best and the two soon form a close bond.

I always thought this was just another good sports movie, but it's so much more then that. Million Dollar Baby is one of my favorite sports movies of all time now, up there with Moneyball. Clint Eastwood's direction is absolutely perfect, it fits the tone perfect, while you don't even really notice it. The performances of everybody are incredible, Hilary Swank deserved that Oscar, Morgan Freeman is doing Morgan Freeman things was his voice, so that's always a win and Clint Eastwood is probably my favorite of them all, that last shot with him hanging over the bed is devastating. The editing is literally perfection and the score subtle, but impactful. The boxing scenes are not the most important thing of this movie, something I really appreciated, a new fresh take on a sports movie. This movie has one of the most powerful ending frames I have ever seen, especially with that last line said by Morgan Freeman. Million Dollar Baby is so much more then just the rise and fall of a boxer, it's about the connection that two broken people build-up, it's about the hard conclusion of life and dead and it's about the stories that get made between those moments, great film!","5c4811d2-2547-4f93-a690-8af3e73ebf54",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2023-06-08","casnien v","RT","6b4ff4a3-5534-4214-a7f3-bff8bedecb7f"
