4.5,"This is indeed a well made, well acted and very compelling drama. However, for all its emotional intensity, I'm not sure it counts as entertainment. Personally I found it very sad and depressing to see the fatal consequences boxing had on a determined young woman trying to make something of her disadvantaged start in life. At the end I felt terrible, thinking that boxing should be banned and that American society needs major social reform for allowing such events to happen. For me it was like going to a funeral, or watching the news. I don't like films that make me feel down, which is why I gave it 50%. If I'd have known how it would make me feel I would not have wanted to watch it.","2d015995-d3be-4376-b76a-56bb2cf1475d",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2023-11-13","Test T","RT","9c61a1b8-8383-4f20-8f81-7a3b767c4380"
